1
00:02:04,094 --> 00:02:08,934
No living creature was
harmed during the filming.

2
00:02:09,030 --> 00:02:11,880
Episode 78

3
00:02:12,031 --> 00:02:14,181
You have done many treacheries.

4
00:02:14,554 --> 00:02:17,394
You made my people, my brother...

5
00:02:18,206 --> 00:02:20,806
and even the sultan turn back on me.

6
00:02:21,826 --> 00:02:25,076
You are biting more than you can chew.

7
00:02:25,643 --> 00:02:32,143
You will pay for your insolence with
your people and tribe.

8
00:02:34,972 --> 00:02:39,312
But, your alps first.

9
00:02:42,796 --> 00:02:45,246
What are you saying.

10
00:02:46,198 --> 00:02:50,958
Setting a trap for the Seljuk vizier...

11
00:02:51,030 --> 00:02:53,690
and drawing your weapons, huh?

12
00:02:55,409 --> 00:02:58,089
You are walking up to your death, Osman.

13
00:03:03,397 --> 00:03:05,707
Stop there, Konur!

14
00:03:09,417 --> 00:03:11,137
Stay there!

15
00:03:16,765 --> 00:03:18,415
We have your alps.

16
00:03:22,330 --> 00:03:24,260
Don't make a mistake, Osman.

17
00:03:24,652 --> 00:03:26,262
Or they'll be killed.

18
00:03:26,523 --> 00:03:28,213
My alps!

19
00:03:30,856 --> 00:03:32,336
Ya Allah!

20
00:04:16,475 --> 00:04:18,105
Are my alps alive?

21
00:04:18,142 --> 00:04:19,882
It depends on you, Osman Bey.

22
00:04:20,171 --> 00:04:21,611
Speak.

23
00:04:23,090 --> 00:04:24,740
Let Vizier Alemşah go.

24
00:04:32,136 --> 00:04:33,136
If...

25
00:04:34,733 --> 00:04:37,373
If you touch them...

26
00:04:39,008 --> 00:04:44,118
I'll kill the vizier first, and
you last.

27
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:50,350
Enough, Osman. Lower your weapon.

28
00:04:50,992 --> 00:04:54,712
Lower, so that I can behead
you only.

29
00:05:01,903 --> 00:05:03,813
Let me go!

30
00:05:04,098 --> 00:05:05,708
Let us go!

31
00:05:07,586 --> 00:05:09,366
My bey!

32
00:05:11,165 --> 00:05:13,255
My bey! We are here!

33
00:05:13,514 --> 00:05:15,354
My bey!

34
00:05:15,354 --> 00:05:17,874
-Alps!
-We are here, my bey.

35
00:05:27,196 --> 00:05:28,666
Step back.

36
00:05:30,663 --> 00:05:32,403
Step back!

37
00:05:37,841 --> 00:05:39,531
Now, move!

38
00:05:46,277 --> 00:05:47,627
Soldiers!

39
00:05:51,283 --> 00:05:53,373
My bey! My bey!

40
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:55,067
Brothers! Are you well?

41
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:58,500
We are, my bey.

42
00:06:05,711 --> 00:06:07,531
Your alps are alive.

43
00:06:07,849 --> 00:06:09,609
Let Vizier Alemşah go.

44
00:06:11,130 --> 00:06:12,870
Or we'll kill them all.

45
00:06:13,539 --> 00:06:15,409
My bey, kill him!

46
00:06:15,559 --> 00:06:18,859
Don't think about us, my bey.
Kill the traitor!

47
00:06:25,257 --> 00:06:26,497
Osman!

48
00:06:39,923 --> 00:06:41,863
Brother, what are you doing?

49
00:06:42,204 --> 00:06:47,244
I'm holding the head of your partner,
Gündüz Bey.

50
00:06:48,546 --> 00:06:50,316
Don't, Osman.

51
00:06:52,929 --> 00:06:56,309
If you kill the vizier, there is no
turning back, Osman.

52
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:02,175
Think for your alps.

53
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:07,480
Think for your tribe,
your tribe!

54
00:07:08,419 --> 00:07:11,559
For my tribe, for my people...

55
00:07:12,898 --> 00:07:16,168
should I be with a traitor like you?

56
00:07:17,886 --> 00:07:20,586
You are disobeying the sultan's
orders!

57
00:07:22,231 --> 00:07:23,581
Don't.

58
00:07:26,413 --> 00:07:29,073
Look, Osman.
Surrender.

59
00:07:30,093 --> 00:07:31,853
The sultan likes you.

60
00:07:32,174 --> 00:07:34,614
Go to his presence and explain
yourself.

61
00:07:35,153 --> 00:07:37,573
My cause is the cause of
the Turks.

62
00:07:39,941 --> 00:07:41,871
This is such a sacred cause that...

63
00:07:43,674 --> 00:07:46,834
there is no need to explain
it to anyone.

64
00:07:52,332 --> 00:07:54,052
But...

65
00:07:56,178 --> 00:07:58,068
even you failed to understand it.

66
00:07:58,963 --> 00:08:00,433
Brother.

67
00:08:05,115 --> 00:08:07,405
Don't, take another step.

68
00:08:13,655 --> 00:08:16,915
I never miss an opportunity...

69
00:08:17,595 --> 00:08:21,791
to kill you, Gündüz Bey.

70
00:08:29,481 --> 00:08:32,030
Or, just go...

71
00:08:32,965 --> 00:08:34,184
go...

72
00:08:37,914 --> 00:08:39,664
Brother...

73
00:08:43,410 --> 00:08:45,141
Osman.

74
00:08:45,843 --> 00:08:49,783
You will pay for what you've done.

75
00:08:51,126 --> 00:08:55,756
But you will never take my life.

76
00:08:58,798 --> 00:09:01,448
Because you are merciful, Osman.

77
00:09:02,483 --> 00:09:06,853
You can't sacrifice your brother
or your alps.

78
00:09:08,625 --> 00:09:10,823
My bey, kill him.

79
00:09:10,823 --> 00:09:13,243
Don't let him speak, my bey!

80
00:09:19,945 --> 00:09:22,295
Your alps don't care about
their lives.

81
00:09:23,329 --> 00:09:25,719
Gündüz Bey is brave.

82
00:09:27,854 --> 00:09:29,914
What about your tribe?

83
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:36,160
If he kills me...

84
00:09:36,515 --> 00:09:38,835
Konur, Ferman!

85
00:09:40,327 --> 00:09:42,997
Turn Kayı Tribe into hell!

86
00:09:47,215 --> 00:09:49,635
Don't leave a single tent unburnt...

87
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:53,710
and a single head not beheaded!

88
00:09:54,950 --> 00:09:56,349
Orhan...

89
00:09:56,349 --> 00:09:57,869
I will--

90
00:09:58,382 --> 00:10:02,792
Of course, if Osman bey doesn't
do the mistake...

91
00:10:04,009 --> 00:10:05,989
Not for what you've done...

92
00:10:07,083 --> 00:10:10,643
even for just saying these things,
I'll rip you apart.

93
00:10:16,059 --> 00:10:17,719
But...

94
00:10:20,749 --> 00:10:22,129
but...

95
00:10:29,722 --> 00:10:31,392
Not now.

96
00:10:33,989 --> 00:10:35,739
Wait.

97
00:10:37,564 --> 00:10:40,124
Wait, Vizier Alemşah.

98
00:10:47,685 --> 00:10:49,635
Don't do it, my bey!

99
00:11:14,029 --> 00:11:16,689
Not now, not then, Osman.

100
00:11:18,149 --> 00:11:21,019
This is the end for you.

101
00:11:25,102 --> 00:11:27,752
Let me think about tomorrow.

102
00:11:39,390 --> 00:11:40,590
Finally.

103
00:11:41,110 --> 00:11:43,370
Finally, the wolf is in the cage!

104
00:11:46,511 --> 00:11:49,951
And the treacherous lion is
at the edge of my sword.

105
00:11:59,186 --> 00:12:01,876
I'll take Nikola for what he did
to Mari.

106
00:12:02,124 --> 00:12:04,845
Osman wants me to take him in when
he comes to Bilecik.

107
00:12:04,845 --> 00:12:08,995
If we don't act with Osman, they'll
unite to destroy us.

108
00:12:09,959 --> 00:12:11,519
Let's hope that.

109
00:12:15,529 --> 00:12:17,809
Traitors!

110
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:19,879
Look at these lords!

111
00:12:22,648 --> 00:12:26,988
Working together with Osman
to destroy me!

112
00:12:29,552 --> 00:12:33,272
No one will move until Osman thinks that
he has won.

113
00:12:34,451 --> 00:12:36,911
Let him think that he is
victorious.

114
00:12:37,904 --> 00:12:42,964
I'll show him that I'm the greatest
of the helpless.

115
00:12:44,828 --> 00:12:48,388
Now is the time to complete
the missing piece.

116
00:12:50,749 --> 00:12:53,839
Julia, bring Rogatus.

117
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:09,090
Lord Rogatus, run!
We've been betrayed!

118
00:13:13,637 --> 00:13:16,707
Damn it! Nikola!

119
00:13:18,351 --> 00:13:20,571
I'll kill you with my hands.

120
00:13:22,922 --> 00:13:26,572
Kosses, did you like my prisoner?

121
00:13:27,574 --> 00:13:31,294
You never knew which side
to pick.

122
00:13:32,690 --> 00:13:35,970
My side matters not, Nikola.

123
00:13:36,499 --> 00:13:38,879
I will be the one to take your life.

124
00:13:41,938 --> 00:13:44,428
Ours will be put to the dungeon.

125
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:49,060
Kosses, your verdict for the treason...

126
00:13:49,260 --> 00:13:52,620
will be given by the emperor
in Constantinople.

127
00:13:52,889 --> 00:13:54,239
You--

128
00:13:59,251 --> 00:14:02,441
The lords are at the emperor's mercy.

129
00:14:02,956 --> 00:14:04,286
Osman.

130
00:14:10,719 --> 00:14:14,259
But you will be executed...

131
00:14:15,264 --> 00:14:17,344
in this castle.

132
00:14:19,536 --> 00:14:21,826
What are you saying, vizier Alemşah?

133
00:14:21,925 --> 00:14:23,455
What execution?

134
00:14:24,408 --> 00:14:27,218
Don't do this!
You can't do that!

135
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:34,920
My bey! My bey!
My bey!

136
00:14:44,556 --> 00:14:46,686
Brother.

137
00:14:49,443 --> 00:14:52,563
My old friend, let's go.

138
00:14:56,010 --> 00:14:57,280
Take him.

139
00:15:25,077 --> 00:15:27,547
Come, Gündüz Bey.
Come.

140
00:15:28,494 --> 00:15:30,174
We'll talk.

141
00:15:53,441 --> 00:15:55,421
What are you waiting for?
Find him!

142
00:15:56,074 --> 00:15:58,654
Dishonorable!

143
00:15:58,723 --> 00:16:01,073
We'll ask for this.

144
00:16:05,706 --> 00:16:07,216
What are you doing?

145
00:16:09,690 --> 00:16:12,900
There is nothing we can learn from them.

146
00:16:14,382 --> 00:16:16,302
There is no need.

147
00:16:16,418 --> 00:16:20,778
If you had smashed them enough
earlier, it wouldn't happen now.

148
00:16:21,896 --> 00:16:24,676
Do your job well, Konur.

149
00:16:32,502 --> 00:16:34,282
Dishonorable.

150
00:16:47,301 --> 00:16:48,711
Bring him.

151
00:16:58,810 --> 00:17:01,940
-Hang on, brother!
-Stop! Stop!

152
00:17:02,476 --> 00:17:04,826
Let him go!

153
00:17:06,434 --> 00:17:07,983
Weasels!

154
00:17:15,694 --> 00:17:17,234
Let me go!

155
00:17:18,613 --> 00:17:20,512
You vile dog!

156
00:17:27,845 --> 00:17:29,505
Hang on, brother!

157
00:17:33,017 --> 00:17:35,247
You vile dog!

158
00:17:38,543 --> 00:17:40,063
You vile dog!

159
00:18:03,229 --> 00:18:05,029
Hang on, brother!

160
00:18:09,828 --> 00:18:12,068
I will kill you!

161
00:18:13,809 --> 00:18:16,619
You stand up against the vizier, huh?

162
00:18:22,371 --> 00:18:24,631
That's enough for now.

163
00:18:24,805 --> 00:18:26,145
I'll come back.

164
00:18:26,244 --> 00:18:28,894
I save you for the last, Osman.

165
00:18:29,441 --> 00:18:31,921
Don't hold back.

166
00:18:46,147 --> 00:18:47,677
Julia.

167
00:18:47,906 --> 00:18:50,146
What do you mean you couldn't
find him?

168
00:18:51,962 --> 00:18:53,602
We couldn't.

169
00:18:53,602 --> 00:18:55,892
We searched everywhere.

170
00:18:56,253 --> 00:19:00,333
But that treacherous Rogatus ran away.

171
00:19:00,429 --> 00:19:03,159
He can't go anywhere, Julia.

172
00:19:04,110 --> 00:19:05,970
I don't like excuses.

173
00:19:07,053 --> 00:19:08,733
You'll find him.

174
00:19:13,287 --> 00:19:14,607
Don't...

175
00:19:16,183 --> 00:19:19,643
bring me any more bad news.

176
00:19:20,328 --> 00:19:24,588
Sir, as you ordered, Kosses is ready
to go to Constantinople.

177
00:19:24,902 --> 00:19:27,442
I don't want any mistake.

178
00:19:27,522 --> 00:19:29,912
I tasked our best soldiers, sir.

179
00:19:30,006 --> 00:19:32,186
We'll take him there without
a problem.

180
00:19:32,275 --> 00:19:33,925
Good.

181
00:19:39,927 --> 00:19:41,817
Vizier Alemşah.

182
00:19:42,588 --> 00:19:44,348
Osman wasn't right.

183
00:19:45,512 --> 00:19:49,942
But execution?

184
00:19:51,329 --> 00:19:55,379
You know it well, it is written in
Sultan's verdict that...

185
00:19:56,582 --> 00:19:58,952
Osman will be trialed in Konya.

186
00:19:59,361 --> 00:20:00,531
Now.

187
00:20:02,082 --> 00:20:04,192
Even without a trial...

188
00:20:04,596 --> 00:20:06,636
what is a execution?

189
00:20:10,167 --> 00:20:13,057
You witnessed
what happened.

190
00:20:13,910 --> 00:20:18,530
Osman put his sword at the neck
of the Seljuk vizier.

191
00:20:20,078 --> 00:20:24,168
If I wasn't lucky, he would
kill me there.

192
00:20:25,436 --> 00:20:28,406
Of course, it will be punished
with execution.

193
00:20:32,451 --> 00:20:33,791
You are right.

194
00:20:34,813 --> 00:20:37,203
Osman made a great mistake.

195
00:20:38,359 --> 00:20:40,569
But everything should be in order.

196
00:20:42,050 --> 00:20:46,470
What I ask from you is to let
Osman be trialed in Konya.

197
00:20:50,735 --> 00:20:55,095
Is it so important for you
to keep Osman Alive?

198
00:21:06,028 --> 00:21:07,948
Vizier Alemşah.

199
00:21:10,087 --> 00:21:12,267
Osman is my brother.

200
00:21:14,045 --> 00:21:16,905
My father Ertuğrul Ghazi left
him to me.

201
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:20,050
Whatever he does...

202
00:21:21,149 --> 00:21:23,389
if you hurt him...

203
00:21:24,347 --> 00:21:25,877
you'll face me...

204
00:21:27,069 --> 00:21:30,789
and the whole of the Kayı Tribe.

205
00:21:34,678 --> 00:21:36,738
You say so?

206
00:21:48,981 --> 00:21:52,491
There is only one way to save Osman.

207
00:21:53,417 --> 00:21:58,387
But you'll have a great
responsibility.

208
00:22:02,635 --> 00:22:05,555
If you want Osman to live...

209
00:22:07,286 --> 00:22:09,336
you'll become the bey
of the Kayı Tribe.

210
00:22:12,531 --> 00:22:14,491
Not as a regent.

211
00:22:15,205 --> 00:22:17,465
You'll be a real bey.

212
00:22:19,220 --> 00:22:22,280
You'll gather the council and
sit on the throne.

213
00:22:23,647 --> 00:22:27,877
And you'll be my right hand
on these lands.

214
00:22:30,835 --> 00:22:33,285
Can you do this, Gündüz Bey?

215
00:22:47,544 --> 00:22:49,164
I will.

216
00:22:52,507 --> 00:22:53,827
If...

217
00:22:55,433 --> 00:22:57,733
it'll save my brother's life...

218
00:22:59,206 --> 00:23:01,096
I'll do anything.

219
00:23:04,686 --> 00:23:06,516
Vizier Alemşah!

220
00:23:06,991 --> 00:23:09,601
It's the promise of Ertuğrul Ghazi's
son, Gündüz Bey.

221
00:23:10,788 --> 00:23:12,678
I'll do as you want.

222
00:23:23,541 --> 00:23:25,381
Good, then.

223
00:23:25,875 --> 00:23:30,505
Osman will be taken to Konya
to be trialed.

224
00:23:34,857 --> 00:23:36,317
Alright.

225
00:23:36,805 --> 00:23:38,495
If you allow me.

226
00:23:53,832 --> 00:23:56,362
When Osman is this close to death...

227
00:23:56,362 --> 00:23:59,127
we can't let him survive!

228
00:24:00,013 --> 00:24:03,853
Vizier Alemşah, if you won't
be able to do this, I will!

229
00:24:04,198 --> 00:24:06,044
If Osman is taken to Konya...

230
00:24:06,044 --> 00:24:08,404
Calm down, Nikola.

231
00:24:10,204 --> 00:24:12,444
We can't take this risk.

232
00:24:14,085 --> 00:24:17,605
Osman will never be on the road.

233
00:24:20,262 --> 00:24:22,102
He will die here.

234
00:24:39,312 --> 00:24:40,859
Degenerate!

235
00:24:40,859 --> 00:24:43,624
Do you think I won't avenge Gonca?

236
00:24:43,624 --> 00:24:45,464
Do you think?

237
00:24:47,327 --> 00:24:48,847
Osman!

238
00:24:51,787 --> 00:24:53,897
Rogatus ran away.

239
00:24:58,929 --> 00:25:02,509
But you and your soldiers...

240
00:25:03,488 --> 00:25:05,618
will be in pain.

241
00:25:10,892 --> 00:25:12,372
Take him out.

242
00:25:16,252 --> 00:25:18,302
Don't touch him!

243
00:25:28,552 --> 00:25:30,872
Take me and leave my bey!

244
00:25:31,350 --> 00:25:33,080
Don't touch my bey!

245
00:25:35,194 --> 00:25:37,659
Come at me!

246
00:25:37,659 --> 00:25:40,739
Come at me, degenerates!

247
00:25:48,081 --> 00:25:50,151
If we get freed...

248
00:25:50,853 --> 00:25:53,363
you'll prefer hell...

249
00:25:54,202 --> 00:25:56,392
to what we'll do to you.

250
00:25:58,276 --> 00:26:00,706
Whip him good.

251
00:26:01,304 --> 00:26:05,884
Until he can't dream of things
he can't do.

252
00:26:21,456 --> 00:26:23,206
Let my bey go!

253
00:26:28,997 --> 00:26:30,787
Hit!

254
00:26:32,048 --> 00:26:33,328
Hang on, my bey!

255
00:26:34,437 --> 00:26:35,887
Degenerates!

256
00:26:37,027 --> 00:26:38,637
Hit!

257
00:26:45,564 --> 00:26:46,864
Osman.

258
00:26:47,950 --> 00:26:49,910
Osman. Osman.

259
00:26:50,067 --> 00:26:51,727
Osman!

260
00:26:52,367 --> 00:26:53,937
Osman!

261
00:26:58,137 --> 00:27:00,317
Osman! Osman!

262
00:27:00,439 --> 00:27:02,359
Bala, my girl?

263
00:27:04,671 --> 00:27:06,189
-Bala!
-Osman!

264
00:27:06,189 --> 00:27:08,559
Bala, wake up!

265
00:27:08,996 --> 00:27:11,426
Bala, wake up, my girl!

266
00:27:12,371 --> 00:27:14,861
Mother! Mother!
Osman!

267
00:27:14,861 --> 00:27:16,836
Calm down, my girl.

268
00:27:16,950 --> 00:27:19,380
Bala Hatun. My lady, are you alright?

269
00:27:23,877 --> 00:27:25,867
It was a dream, mother.

270
00:27:26,129 --> 00:27:27,695
Bring water, Zehra.

271
00:27:27,695 --> 00:27:30,185
It was a dream.
Osman was in darkness.

272
00:27:30,539 --> 00:27:32,479
I don't feel good.

273
00:27:32,848 --> 00:27:35,328
What if they hurt Osman?

274
00:27:37,051 --> 00:27:39,481
Drink this.
Drink it.

275
00:27:42,090 --> 00:27:45,440
It was a nightmare. You can't find
meanings in a nightmare.

276
00:27:45,534 --> 00:27:47,424
Be at ease.

277
00:27:52,721 --> 00:27:54,551
Thank you, Zehra.

278
00:27:57,297 --> 00:28:00,587
Osman is alright.
Be at ease.

279
00:28:15,330 --> 00:28:17,840
Vizier Alemşah wants Osman at
his presence.

280
00:28:24,229 --> 00:28:26,429
Tie him up!

281
00:28:27,212 --> 00:28:28,992
We don't know what he'll do.

282
00:28:32,112 --> 00:28:34,690
Bilecik Castle.

283
00:28:34,690 --> 00:28:37,090
I'll make you pay...

284
00:28:37,199 --> 00:28:39,869
for what you did to Mari.

285
00:28:40,318 --> 00:28:41,988
Nikola.

286
00:28:42,303 --> 00:28:45,933
So, the reason for this betreyal
is your stupid sister, huh?

287
00:28:46,576 --> 00:28:49,316
You convinced Rogatus too!

288
00:29:05,522 --> 00:29:08,782
This insolence must be because
of your helplessness.

289
00:29:09,358 --> 00:29:14,058
After all, if I was on my way to
the emperor to be trialed...

290
00:29:14,065 --> 00:29:17,195
I would be mad like you.

291
00:29:17,407 --> 00:29:21,349
But don't worry. You won't
be alone. After I get Rogatus...

292
00:29:21,349 --> 00:29:23,719
I'll send him to you.

293
00:29:26,677 --> 00:29:28,777
For my burnt market...

294
00:29:30,215 --> 00:29:33,009
I have Harmankaya...

295
00:29:33,009 --> 00:29:34,679
for myself!

296
00:29:36,051 --> 00:29:37,291
Mine!

297
00:29:45,826 --> 00:29:48,806
I, Aya Nikola...

298
00:29:48,806 --> 00:29:52,116
the lord of İnegöl and Harmankaya!

299
00:29:56,712 --> 00:30:01,882
You will beg me to kill you.

300
00:30:02,987 --> 00:30:05,047
Did you hear me?

301
00:30:06,057 --> 00:30:08,497
I will kill you.

302
00:30:10,170 --> 00:30:12,550
A nothing!

303
00:30:13,090 --> 00:30:15,570
What can he do to me?

304
00:30:34,047 --> 00:30:36,397
Welcome, Osman Bey.

305
00:30:41,889 --> 00:30:43,659
Come closer.

306
00:30:59,518 --> 00:31:04,408
You became these lands that your
father Ertuğrul Ghazi left.

307
00:31:06,640 --> 00:31:10,470
He had older brothers,
an uncle...

308
00:31:11,554 --> 00:31:14,334
if they chose him as the leader...

309
00:31:15,498 --> 00:31:19,238
he must be a great man, I would say.

310
00:31:22,386 --> 00:31:26,296
But you turned out to be
quite a fool, Osman.

311
00:31:29,165 --> 00:31:31,985
What righteous move,
or virtue...

312
00:31:32,836 --> 00:31:35,856
do you find to be foolish?

313
00:31:36,332 --> 00:31:38,112
Tell me.

314
00:31:38,393 --> 00:31:42,733
You don't see the power balances.

315
00:31:46,222 --> 00:31:48,052
Who am I?

316
00:31:49,733 --> 00:31:52,633
The shadow of the Seljuks!

317
00:31:55,581 --> 00:31:57,591
You are right.

318
00:31:58,798 --> 00:32:00,538
You are right.

319
00:32:01,842 --> 00:32:06,482
Sultan Mesud is the sun.
You are his shadow.

320
00:32:09,917 --> 00:32:14,197
You exist when he does,
and not when he doesn't.

321
00:32:17,872 --> 00:32:22,792
Our existence doesn't depend on anyone
but Allah!

322
00:32:24,717 --> 00:32:28,207
We aren't the shadow of
anyone.

323
00:32:33,210 --> 00:32:35,900
You disobeyed the state's orders.

324
00:32:36,230 --> 00:32:38,540
You drew your weapon against
your vizier.

325
00:32:41,210 --> 00:32:43,770
You will pay for it all.

326
00:32:44,407 --> 00:32:46,827
After I talk to Sultan Mesud...

327
00:32:47,800 --> 00:32:49,770
he'll see the truth.

328
00:32:50,915 --> 00:32:56,015
He'll be sorry that he gave someone
like you such a position.

329
00:33:09,537 --> 00:33:11,097
Osman.

330
00:33:12,105 --> 00:33:15,665
Who told you that you will
go to Konya?

331
00:33:21,846 --> 00:33:23,856
Here. Here.

332
00:33:23,965 --> 00:33:25,435
In Bilecik.

333
00:33:26,484 --> 00:33:28,664
You will be...

334
00:33:30,464 --> 00:33:32,864
hung!

335
00:33:47,557 --> 00:33:49,727
And not only you.

336
00:33:51,195 --> 00:33:53,085
All your alps.

337
00:34:11,879 --> 00:34:14,099
I'll never kneel!

338
00:34:14,636 --> 00:34:17,126
No one can make me kneel!

339
00:34:17,639 --> 00:34:19,339
No one!

340
00:34:26,830 --> 00:34:30,190
Setting an ambush to the
state's vizier, huh?

341
00:34:31,286 --> 00:34:34,407
Drawing a weapon against
the vizier, huh?

342
00:34:36,179 --> 00:34:39,090
Take him away!

343
00:34:40,039 --> 00:34:41,569
You!

344
00:34:44,099 --> 00:34:48,109
You are neither the state nor the
vizier of the state!

345
00:34:48,864 --> 00:34:51,125
You baseborn!

346
00:34:51,799 --> 00:34:54,279
There is treachery in your blood.

347
00:34:57,512 --> 00:35:02,372
But sooner or later,
the truth will be revealed!

348
00:35:03,889 --> 00:35:08,339
Either with us or without us!

349
00:35:10,669 --> 00:35:13,609
Your end will come!

350
00:35:14,336 --> 00:35:16,586
Your end will come!

351
00:35:25,158 --> 00:35:28,708
Osman is in my way, Konur.

352
00:35:29,739 --> 00:35:35,739
We'll hang him tomorrow. His death
will be good for Gündüz and the Kayı.

353
00:35:37,509 --> 00:35:39,759
Gündüz Bey won't allow this.

354
00:35:43,021 --> 00:35:44,681
Do I need a permission?

355
00:35:45,845 --> 00:35:48,365
What we say happens.

356
00:35:52,091 --> 00:35:55,391
We'll tell Gündüz Bey that
we caught him running away.

357
00:35:56,203 --> 00:36:00,913
And we hung him to not
provoke the lords.

358
00:36:02,131 --> 00:36:07,191
My vizier, the sultan's verdict.
He makes sure that he wants him in Konya.

359
00:36:08,964 --> 00:36:12,394
Let the sultan send orders from
his throne.

360
00:36:13,064 --> 00:36:16,764
The sword was at my neck, Konur!

361
00:36:18,907 --> 00:36:21,017
My decision is final.

362
00:36:21,165 --> 00:36:23,225
Everything has a price.

363
00:36:24,520 --> 00:36:27,770
This is the price of
revolting against...

364
00:36:27,814 --> 00:36:29,124
Alemşah!

365
00:36:31,356 --> 00:36:34,496
As you see fit, my vizier.

366
00:37:11,445 --> 00:37:12,915
Who are you?

367
00:37:14,460 --> 00:37:16,160
What do you want?

368
00:37:18,054 --> 00:37:20,634
Some seek it, some just find it, Rogatus.

369
00:37:28,659 --> 00:37:30,659
We were waiting for Osman Bey.

370
00:37:31,114 --> 00:37:33,424
He would come from here
if anything went wrong.

371
00:37:35,598 --> 00:37:37,208
You...

372
00:37:38,224 --> 00:37:39,694
you are Father Philip.

373
00:37:45,011 --> 00:37:47,001
My name isn't Philip.

374
00:37:47,886 --> 00:37:50,276
We are on the righteous path!

375
00:37:51,953 --> 00:37:55,703
We put our efforts for that only!

376
00:37:57,120 --> 00:37:59,150
I'm Kumral Abdal.

377
00:38:03,153 --> 00:38:05,003
I'm Osman Bey's comrade.

378
00:38:07,168 --> 00:38:09,658
I heard that you are a friend.

379
00:38:12,396 --> 00:38:16,086
Tell me, Rogatus. Why are you running
away from the castle.

380
00:38:16,608 --> 00:38:18,358
Where is Osman Bey?

381
00:38:20,275 --> 00:38:21,895
We were betrayed.

382
00:38:23,749 --> 00:38:26,143
Osman Bey and Kosses are taken
captives.

383
00:38:26,143 --> 00:38:28,023
I ran away.

384
00:38:32,924 --> 00:38:35,184
What? What?

385
00:38:37,871 --> 00:38:39,371
No!

386
00:38:40,729 --> 00:38:43,229
Allah!
Allah!

387
00:38:44,307 --> 00:38:45,987
My bey!

388
00:38:46,471 --> 00:38:47,941
The alps!

389
00:38:50,886 --> 00:38:53,016
Alemşah! Ah!

390
00:38:53,365 --> 00:38:55,285
What tricks have you
pulled again?

391
00:38:56,276 --> 00:38:58,376
What tricks have you pulled
again?

392
00:39:02,087 --> 00:39:05,737
He worked together with Nikola and
bought my soldiers.

393
00:39:06,659 --> 00:39:08,136
My soldiers!

394
00:39:08,136 --> 00:39:11,056
The one who took Prophet Joseph
out of that dungeon...

395
00:39:13,261 --> 00:39:15,391
will surely take Osman Bey too!

396
00:39:22,319 --> 00:39:23,929
We shouldn't stand here.

397
00:39:25,756 --> 00:39:27,376
We are in the open now.

398
00:39:28,689 --> 00:39:30,539
We need to hide.

399
00:39:32,518 --> 00:39:33,988
Come on.

400
00:39:34,293 --> 00:39:35,633
Come on.

401
00:39:39,971 --> 00:39:41,851
A wolf can't be a captive.

402
00:39:45,435 --> 00:39:48,185
While we were trying to save
our brother...

403
00:39:49,225 --> 00:39:51,345
he throws himself
to a well!

404
00:39:53,491 --> 00:39:55,921
Speak it out!

405
00:39:58,484 --> 00:40:00,564
Complete your sentence!

406
00:40:03,525 --> 00:40:04,785
Mother!

407
00:40:05,689 --> 00:40:08,179
Osman tried to kill the vizier!

408
00:40:10,820 --> 00:40:13,760
An execution verdict is given!

409
00:40:18,410 --> 00:40:21,080
Do you hear what you say, Gündüz Bey?

410
00:40:21,738 --> 00:40:24,308
-What execution?
-Execution! Execution!

411
00:40:24,542 --> 00:40:27,352
But hold on!

412
00:40:28,093 --> 00:40:30,813
We'll see what other troubles Osman
will bring upon him.

413
00:40:32,684 --> 00:40:35,314
While we were trying to
protect our brother...

414
00:40:35,410 --> 00:40:38,640
and expect him to control
himself...

415
00:40:38,661 --> 00:40:42,461
Would he? No! He runs to
even greater troubles!

416
00:40:44,233 --> 00:40:47,673
What are you doing when your
brother is fighting the world, Gündüz?

417
00:40:48,201 --> 00:40:51,651
Are you getting mad at your
brother there?

418
00:40:51,651 --> 00:40:53,151
Mother!

419
00:40:57,120 --> 00:40:59,280
For my brother's life...

420
00:40:59,681 --> 00:41:01,591
I put myself there!

421
00:41:02,709 --> 00:41:04,529
I saved him from the rope!

422
00:41:10,213 --> 00:41:12,343
Bilecik Castle.

423
00:41:29,888 --> 00:41:32,908
Jesus Christ heard our prayers!

424
00:41:34,124 --> 00:41:38,004
Osman who killed our soldiers
will be hung at Bilecik today!

425
00:41:43,552 --> 00:41:45,152
People!

426
00:41:45,648 --> 00:41:47,878
The greatest heathen...

427
00:41:48,208 --> 00:41:50,358
the greatest evil...

428
00:41:50,878 --> 00:41:53,328
Osman and his alps will
be hung today!

429
00:41:54,319 --> 00:41:57,069
Sacred children of Jesus Christ!

430
00:41:57,855 --> 00:42:00,235
We'll take our revenge!

431
00:42:24,357 --> 00:42:25,537
Ferman.

432
00:42:27,350 --> 00:42:29,430
Nothing will go wrong.

433
00:42:30,265 --> 00:42:33,385
Osman will die here today and here.

434
00:42:34,008 --> 00:42:35,698
He will, my vizier.

435
00:42:35,834 --> 00:42:38,204
Everything is prepared as you want.

436
00:42:48,429 --> 00:42:50,709
Sacred children of Jesus Christ!

437
00:42:51,356 --> 00:42:53,706
Our revenge will be taken.

438
00:42:53,945 --> 00:42:56,675
Osman who killed our soldiers...

439
00:42:56,701 --> 00:42:59,301
Still no trace of Rogatus?

440
00:43:02,176 --> 00:43:04,046
We still haven't found him.

441
00:43:06,795 --> 00:43:09,445
Find Rogatus, Julia.

442
00:43:10,127 --> 00:43:12,497
Do everything for that.

443
00:43:21,934 --> 00:43:23,914
Vizier listened to us...

444
00:43:25,248 --> 00:43:28,068
and took the rope away from
Osman's neck.

445
00:43:31,173 --> 00:43:32,663
Look at this.

446
00:43:32,958 --> 00:43:35,668
That devil wouldn't work without
a return.

447
00:43:36,431 --> 00:43:38,661
Did he take it off with
a single word of yours?

448
00:43:40,757 --> 00:43:44,507
Speak! What did he want from
you in return, Gündüz?

449
00:43:46,116 --> 00:43:49,126
What did you give the vizier that
he left Osman?

450
00:43:53,737 --> 00:43:55,727
As the vizier says...

451
00:43:57,099 --> 00:44:00,329
from now, I'll be the right hand
of Alemşah in these lands.

452
00:44:03,680 --> 00:44:05,230
With his order...

453
00:44:07,399 --> 00:44:09,339
the council will be gathered.

454
00:44:13,689 --> 00:44:15,569
The tribe has a bey, Gündüz Bey.

455
00:44:16,217 --> 00:44:18,297
What are you talking about?

456
00:44:19,506 --> 00:44:21,666
I will never allow this!

457
00:44:24,171 --> 00:44:26,891
Because you sat on the throne
for a few days...

458
00:44:27,723 --> 00:44:30,783
you forgot the owner of the throne!

459
00:44:32,008 --> 00:44:37,518
But we'll remind you! The throne you
sit on belongs to Osman Bey!

460
00:44:41,735 --> 00:44:46,485
This tribe can't survive any other
fight for the throne.

461
00:44:48,555 --> 00:44:50,995
Don't do this to your brother,
Gündüz Bey.

462
00:44:51,073 --> 00:44:53,073
And what do you want?

463
00:44:55,664 --> 00:44:58,444
Our tribe will be burnt down...

464
00:44:59,377 --> 00:45:01,897
and people will be killed, is that it?

465
00:45:02,952 --> 00:45:05,162
There were no other choice.

466
00:45:07,570 --> 00:45:09,620
And not only me.

467
00:45:13,641 --> 00:45:15,461
Get mad at Osman too.

468
00:45:16,697 --> 00:45:18,547
If he didn't ran away...

469
00:45:19,252 --> 00:45:21,452
if he went to the Sultan...

470
00:45:22,137 --> 00:45:24,357
none of this would
ever happen!

471
00:45:28,285 --> 00:45:31,725
Don't I know you a bit?

472
00:45:33,144 --> 00:45:36,414
The Gündüz I know wouldn't do this.

473
00:45:37,266 --> 00:45:39,726
He would stand behind
his brother.

474
00:45:42,355 --> 00:45:43,975
Tell me.

475
00:45:44,253 --> 00:45:46,183
Who is this?

476
00:45:46,298 --> 00:45:49,018
That can't stand behind his brother.

477
00:45:52,413 --> 00:45:54,963
Mother, don't.

478
00:45:55,179 --> 00:45:58,919
Gündüz Bey does what he does
for us. Don't you see?

479
00:46:04,800 --> 00:46:10,030
I'll not allow this tribe left from my
father to suffer any more!

480
00:46:15,435 --> 00:46:19,325
From now, if anyone goes against
my word...

481
00:46:21,510 --> 00:46:24,590
I'll consider it against
the bey's words.

482
00:46:37,797 --> 00:46:39,617
Gündüz Bey.

483
00:46:42,689 --> 00:46:45,809
See where you are going before
taking a step.

484
00:46:46,733 --> 00:46:48,933
Don't regret it later.

485
00:46:50,445 --> 00:46:53,155
I know where I step on well, mother.

486
00:47:05,253 --> 00:47:07,613
Bilecik Castle

487
00:47:09,522 --> 00:47:11,362
My valiants.

488
00:47:15,821 --> 00:47:17,461
My alps.

489
00:47:20,608 --> 00:47:22,218
I'm a witness.

490
00:47:22,970 --> 00:47:28,200
You walked on Allah's way.

491
00:47:31,383 --> 00:47:33,923
For the prophet's cause...

492
00:47:34,738 --> 00:47:36,578
you turned your swords...

493
00:47:37,871 --> 00:47:42,121
into Zülfikar and used them on
the heathens!

494
00:47:42,928 --> 00:47:48,748
To tremble the whole world with
the sound of 'Allahu Akbar'...

495
00:47:49,363 --> 00:47:53,953
you took many difficult paths
with me.

496
00:47:55,315 --> 00:47:56,855
Now...

497
00:47:57,870 --> 00:48:00,420
now Yezid will stay a Yezid.

498
00:48:02,478 --> 00:48:04,488
And if our destiny...

499
00:48:06,118 --> 00:48:10,328
is to fall martyr, like the favorite of
our good prophet...

500
00:48:11,090 --> 00:48:15,730
our minister Hüseyin...

501
00:48:17,700 --> 00:48:19,780
it's a grace!

502
00:48:20,310 --> 00:48:22,570
We'll be glad!

503
00:48:22,677 --> 00:48:25,927
-Praise Allah, my bey.
-Praise Allah.

504
00:48:27,084 --> 00:48:28,894
Praise Allah.

505
00:48:34,722 --> 00:48:36,532
My commanders in Bilecik.

506
00:48:38,050 --> 00:48:40,320
Nikola must've bought them.

507
00:48:40,860 --> 00:48:45,520
But there are loyal ones among them.
Who can't be bought with money.

508
00:48:45,709 --> 00:48:48,299
But it's impossible to reach them now.

509
00:48:49,066 --> 00:48:50,496
It's the humans...

510
00:48:51,473 --> 00:48:53,593
they see every opportunity
as if it's from them.

511
00:48:55,385 --> 00:48:57,315
Insolent...

512
00:48:59,266 --> 00:49:01,566
needs to know his place first.

513
00:49:05,944 --> 00:49:07,874
Not you.

514
00:49:08,409 --> 00:49:10,219
The humans.

515
00:49:12,706 --> 00:49:15,126
Allah shows many ways.

516
00:49:15,969 --> 00:49:18,949
When the human can't see them,
he can't reach them.

517
00:49:22,052 --> 00:49:26,702
And if you are so sure of their
loyalty...

518
00:49:27,882 --> 00:49:30,022
I will bring them to you.

519
00:49:32,055 --> 00:49:34,485
They won't say no after
seeing me.

520
00:49:34,586 --> 00:49:37,936
If they are as loyal
as you said...

521
00:49:38,974 --> 00:49:41,344
they won't care who's
calling them.

522
00:49:41,499 --> 00:49:42,819
Lord.

523
00:49:45,434 --> 00:49:47,684
They'll come for you.

524
00:49:53,201 --> 00:49:54,861
I'm grateful.

525
00:49:56,769 --> 00:49:58,819
For everything.

526
00:50:01,161 --> 00:50:03,341
If you can bring my commanders here...

527
00:50:03,369 --> 00:50:05,539
you will learn the news from Osman.

528
00:50:10,317 --> 00:50:11,837
Julia.

529
00:50:12,794 --> 00:50:18,824
Because of her betrayal, Osman is being
kept by Nicola and the vizier.

530
00:50:21,478 --> 00:50:23,578
They will kill him.

531
00:50:24,273 --> 00:50:26,083
They will not let him live.

532
00:50:26,535 --> 00:50:28,125
He will die in vain.

533
00:50:34,774 --> 00:50:37,814
If Osman Bey dies, he will be a martyr.

534
00:50:38,942 --> 00:50:41,112
For the martyrs, it is said that;

535
00:50:41,605 --> 00:50:44,925
"As for those who are killed in the
way of Allah..."

536
00:50:45,285 --> 00:50:48,905
Allah will not let their deeds
be in vain."

537
00:50:51,894 --> 00:50:54,064
Martyr's blood is not shed in vain,
Tekfur.

538
00:50:59,100 --> 00:51:01,030
But I know that...

539
00:51:01,825 --> 00:51:03,715
If I become a martyr...

540
00:51:04,739 --> 00:51:07,999
our case will not bow down.

541
00:51:08,496 --> 00:51:10,666
Even if we die...

542
00:51:10,975 --> 00:51:13,645
the love and faith of Allah...

543
00:51:14,065 --> 00:51:18,175
will always bloom in the hearts of
our children.

544
00:51:19,384 --> 00:51:25,154
Our brave sons will carry on the Islam
that we handed over.

545
00:51:25,832 --> 00:51:27,312
I hope so.

546
00:51:29,591 --> 00:51:31,631
My alps.

547
00:51:32,423 --> 00:51:34,743
The brave alps of Kayi tribe!

548
00:51:36,485 --> 00:51:38,645
I give you all of my blessings.

549
00:51:43,757 --> 00:51:46,517
May Allah give you his blessings too.

550
00:51:47,951 --> 00:51:49,851
I forgive you for all of your faults.

551
00:51:51,957 --> 00:51:54,537
-Forgive me for all of my faults too.
-We forgive you.

552
00:51:54,673 --> 00:51:56,683
We forgive you, my Bey.

553
00:51:57,367 --> 00:51:59,007
We forgive you, my Bey.

554
00:51:59,473 --> 00:52:00,943
We forgive you.

555
00:52:02,502 --> 00:52:05,142
We forgive you, my Bey.

556
00:52:07,527 --> 00:52:09,107
What did you do as a fault?

557
00:52:12,061 --> 00:52:14,071
We give all of our blessings, my Bey.

558
00:52:17,490 --> 00:52:18,830
All of our blessings.

559
00:52:25,017 --> 00:52:28,687
If Osman Bey dies, you will not have
a leader.

560
00:52:30,483 --> 00:52:34,013
How can you be so calm in this
situation?

561
00:52:34,844 --> 00:52:37,454
Do you know Hadhrat Hamza?

562
00:52:39,227 --> 00:52:40,857
Hadhrat Ali?

563
00:52:41,290 --> 00:52:42,920
Hadhrat Osman?

564
00:52:43,134 --> 00:52:47,274
Do you know Zeyd Bin Harise?
Abdullah bin Revaha?

565
00:52:47,530 --> 00:52:50,380
Do you know Cafer bin Ebu Talib?

566
00:52:50,647 --> 00:52:52,917
Do you know Hadhrat Hüseyin?

567
00:52:56,108 --> 00:52:58,638
I don't know. I heard them for
the first time.

568
00:53:01,699 --> 00:53:03,749
How can you know?

569
00:53:04,321 --> 00:53:06,351
Of course, you don't know.

570
00:53:07,360 --> 00:53:09,320
They are such people that...

571
00:53:10,876 --> 00:53:12,766
I would give my life for them.

572
00:53:15,868 --> 00:53:20,388
They were from the stars of the sky,
the sky of Hadhrat Muhammed.

573
00:53:25,454 --> 00:53:27,764
They were the closest ones to him.

574
00:53:29,783 --> 00:53:31,663
Especially, Hüseyin.

575
00:53:32,008 --> 00:53:33,598
He was so precious.

576
00:53:34,809 --> 00:53:37,249
All of them were martyred
for Allah.

577
00:53:40,648 --> 00:53:42,918
We are still feeling the pain.

578
00:53:44,035 --> 00:53:46,825
Such a pain, it is such a pain.

579
00:53:49,997 --> 00:53:53,207
But their deaths are for Allah.

580
00:53:53,308 --> 00:53:54,898
That's why we don't woe.

581
00:53:55,871 --> 00:54:00,701
After them, many people died
in the way of Allah.

582
00:54:01,050 --> 00:54:03,940
If Osman Bey will be a martyr for
this purpose...

583
00:54:04,083 --> 00:54:05,793
let him be.

584
00:54:06,249 --> 00:54:09,219
If we will be in grief, let us be.

585
00:54:09,312 --> 00:54:12,372
We will not woe.

586
00:54:12,534 --> 00:54:16,144
It is enough for us as long as the
belief in Allah lasts forever.

587
00:54:18,854 --> 00:54:20,304
You...

588
00:54:23,628 --> 00:54:25,018
Turks...

589
00:54:27,425 --> 00:54:30,415
you amaze me more and more every day.

590
00:54:32,481 --> 00:54:35,091
I never thought you would think like this.

591
00:54:35,422 --> 00:54:37,252
Allah!

592
00:54:49,350 --> 00:54:54,160
The time of every death is certain.

593
00:54:57,895 --> 00:55:01,675
But it's not the right
time for you, Osman Bey.

594
00:55:03,356 --> 00:55:06,016
Martyrdom is forbidden to you for now.

595
00:55:08,164 --> 00:55:10,644
You will not experience this now.

596
00:55:13,969 --> 00:55:15,869
It is forbidden, Osman Bey.

597
00:55:25,123 --> 00:55:26,483
You...

598
00:55:30,370 --> 00:55:31,850
will...

599
00:55:37,539 --> 00:55:39,339
establish a state first.

600
00:55:42,689 --> 00:55:44,049
Firstly...

601
00:55:47,827 --> 00:55:49,767
you will establish a state.

602
00:55:54,146 --> 00:55:55,966
The secret is solved.

603
00:55:57,755 --> 00:56:00,135
The secret is solved.

604
00:56:21,322 --> 00:56:23,482
Are you ready to die?

605
00:56:26,498 --> 00:56:29,578
I will watch with great pleasure...

606
00:56:29,775 --> 00:56:32,045
as you swing on the rope.

607
00:56:36,357 --> 00:56:38,537
If we die...

608
00:56:39,758 --> 00:56:41,848
we will be martyrs.

609
00:56:44,868 --> 00:56:47,108
We are not afraid of the rope.

610
00:56:48,832 --> 00:56:51,342
But if we live...

611
00:56:52,555 --> 00:56:54,915
dig yourself a grave...

612
00:56:55,365 --> 00:56:56,925
and go inside.

613
00:57:00,016 --> 00:57:01,606
Soldiers!

614
00:57:24,591 --> 00:57:27,491
The Castle of Harmankaya

615
00:57:29,762 --> 00:57:31,322
Mari.

616
00:57:36,244 --> 00:57:38,604
Soldiers, get this man out of here!

617
00:57:38,857 --> 00:57:42,567
I'm talking to you. You will not let this
man enter my castle again.

618
00:57:44,564 --> 00:57:48,214
Don't you dare! Don't you dare to
get closer to me, Nicola.

619
00:57:48,626 --> 00:57:52,536
If you try to harm me in this castle, you
will pay a heavy price.

620
00:57:53,452 --> 00:57:55,722
Don't be so sure, Mari.

621
00:57:56,496 --> 00:58:00,126
Because this castle is not yours anymore.

622
00:58:03,985 --> 00:58:06,725
Your lovely brother Koses...

623
00:58:07,078 --> 00:58:10,318
tried to kill the vizier with Osman.

624
00:58:10,650 --> 00:58:14,490
So, Koses is a traitor now.

625
00:58:15,525 --> 00:58:18,695
What do we do in this situation
according to the rules?

626
00:58:19,274 --> 00:58:21,204
We give punishment.

627
00:58:31,769 --> 00:58:33,099
Harmankaya...

628
00:58:35,474 --> 00:58:37,014
is mine now.

629
00:58:37,719 --> 00:58:39,909
What did you do to my brother,
Nicola?

630
00:58:40,067 --> 00:58:44,247
He will talk to the
Emperor, not to me, Mari.

631
00:58:45,735 --> 00:58:50,155
Will you give me this castle without
causing any problem or...

632
00:58:51,313 --> 00:58:55,438
should I come with the soldiers
of the Emperor and...

633
00:58:55,438 --> 00:59:00,178
destroy this place?

634
00:59:00,322 --> 00:59:02,019
What should I do?

635
00:59:02,019 --> 00:59:03,299
Never.

636
00:59:03,877 --> 00:59:05,987
I won't even give you garbage.

637
00:59:08,045 --> 00:59:09,415
Soldiers.

638
00:59:14,361 --> 00:59:17,641
Eventually, Samuel. Get this man
out of here.

639
00:59:18,519 --> 00:59:22,309
Agios Nikola, me and my soldiers
are waiting for your orders.

640
00:59:24,740 --> 00:59:27,000
Soldiers, lower the flags!

641
00:59:29,721 --> 00:59:34,061
No. No! Don't you dare to touch them!
Don't touch!

642
00:59:34,548 --> 00:59:35,998
Don't touch me!

643
00:59:36,019 --> 00:59:37,449
Don't touch me!

644
00:59:37,570 --> 00:59:39,190
Leave me!

645
00:59:51,772 --> 00:59:53,482
How could you do this, traitor?!

646
00:59:53,482 --> 00:59:54,852
Samuel.

647
00:59:55,786 --> 00:59:58,412
Take your most loyal soldiers.

648
00:59:58,412 --> 01:00:01,392
And kill everyone who you
suspect of their loyalty.

649
01:00:02,675 --> 01:00:04,625
I don't want any mistakes.

650
01:00:06,112 --> 01:00:08,772
And also, that new groom.
What was his name?

651
01:00:11,741 --> 01:00:13,401
Turgut.

652
01:00:16,088 --> 01:00:19,648
If he comes to the castle, kill him.

653
01:00:19,648 --> 01:00:23,362
Don't even hesitate. Don't let him
leave this castle alive.

654
01:00:25,561 --> 01:00:27,629
You will never be able to do this,
Nikola.

655
01:00:27,629 --> 01:00:29,549
You will regret what you did!

656
01:00:29,633 --> 01:00:31,473
Shut up, don't talk!

657
01:00:31,619 --> 01:00:34,079
Leave her alone! Don't touch her!

658
01:00:34,868 --> 01:00:36,678
Cornelia!

659
01:00:40,825 --> 01:00:42,295
Argus.

660
01:00:42,701 --> 01:00:44,681
Take Mari to my castle.

661
01:00:45,845 --> 01:00:49,725
I don't like my work being left
unfinished.

662
01:00:50,373 --> 01:00:52,973
We have an issue to finish.

663
01:00:56,178 --> 01:01:00,908
But this time it will not be that easy,
Mari.

664
01:01:14,999 --> 01:01:17,199
You should've died that day.

665
01:01:19,011 --> 01:01:21,951
Now my anger is stronger, Mari.

666
01:01:24,297 --> 01:01:26,537
See you at İnegöl.

667
01:01:33,330 --> 01:01:35,980
The Castle of Bilecik

668
01:02:23,847 --> 01:02:25,967
Osman will be hanged first.

669
01:02:28,958 --> 01:02:31,218
And then, his soldiers.

670
01:03:39,706 --> 01:03:42,406
You came at the most opportune
time, Nikola.

671
01:03:42,442 --> 01:03:46,010
I came here as soon as possible
after I seize the Castle of Harmankaya.

672
01:03:46,010 --> 01:03:48,400
I can't miss such a moment.

673
01:03:48,716 --> 01:03:52,595
You don't know how long I've been
waiting for today, Vizier Alemşah.

674
01:03:52,595 --> 01:03:54,785
Today is my celebration day.

675
01:03:54,837 --> 01:03:58,237
We will see many celebration
days together, Nikola.

676
01:04:25,022 --> 01:04:26,512
Die, die!

677
01:04:40,933 --> 01:04:42,473
Eventually.

678
01:04:42,519 --> 01:04:44,229
Eventually!

679
01:05:10,227 --> 01:05:11,807
Die!

680
01:05:23,268 --> 01:05:25,568
O Allah, the victor!

681
01:05:25,762 --> 01:05:28,292
O Allah, the victor!

682
01:05:33,993 --> 01:05:36,693
Will we wait like this?

683
01:05:36,914 --> 01:05:40,454
After all this, are we going to leave
Osman to the mercy of the Sultan?

684
01:05:41,189 --> 01:05:43,339
Of course, we will not, Bala.

685
01:05:43,734 --> 01:05:45,952
We can't trust Sultan Mesud anymore.

686
01:05:45,952 --> 01:05:49,262
It is the vizier of the Sultan who
brought these matters to us.

687
01:05:50,764 --> 01:05:53,574
There are no alps, what will we do?

688
01:05:53,625 --> 01:05:55,972
I will take the alps that are loyal to
Osman.

689
01:05:55,972 --> 01:05:57,886
We will save Osman in the way of Konya.

690
01:05:57,886 --> 01:06:00,736
You're outnumbered. How will you win?

691
01:06:00,977 --> 01:06:02,817
This time, I will come too.

692
01:06:02,994 --> 01:06:04,734
I will not leave Osman alone.

693
01:06:04,907 --> 01:06:06,777
What are you talking about?

694
01:06:06,953 --> 01:06:09,423
You're entrusted to me by Osman.

695
01:06:09,787 --> 01:06:12,507
I don't want to put both you and your
child in danger.

696
01:06:12,772 --> 01:06:14,752
And our people need a head.

697
01:06:14,869 --> 01:06:17,189
Stay there and take care of them.

698
01:06:38,793 --> 01:06:42,905
Osman attempted evil to break
the friendship...

699
01:06:42,905 --> 01:06:47,935
we established with the Emperor.

700
01:06:48,862 --> 01:06:54,322
He opposed the order of the Seljuk Empire.

701
01:06:55,093 --> 01:06:57,543
Cut it short. Come on, come on!

702
01:07:00,522 --> 01:07:03,412
I, Vizier Alemşah...

703
01:07:04,554 --> 01:07:10,764
I am here to put the ones who
oppose the order in their place.

704
01:07:26,829 --> 01:07:28,279
Whoever tries...

705
01:07:29,005 --> 01:07:33,535
to overshadow the order
established by the Seljuk Empire...

706
01:07:36,637 --> 01:07:38,297
his fate...

707
01:07:41,188 --> 01:07:45,218
will be hanged like Osman.

708
01:07:48,935 --> 01:07:50,585
Now...

709
01:07:50,835 --> 01:07:55,855
you will pay for this rebellion, Osman.

710
01:07:58,812 --> 01:08:01,302
Come on. Come on.

711
01:08:04,113 --> 01:08:10,623
If you had obeyed, that rope
would not be around your neck now.

712
01:08:16,602 --> 01:08:20,462
You tried to kill the vizier of the
Seljuk Empire.

713
01:08:21,090 --> 01:08:24,310
Now, you will pay for this.

714
01:08:25,718 --> 01:08:27,058
Both I and...

715
01:08:28,921 --> 01:08:30,651
my valiants...

716
01:08:33,179 --> 01:08:36,319
prefer to die in the way of Allah...

717
01:08:38,977 --> 01:08:41,216
rather than...

718
01:08:42,524 --> 01:08:44,645
living a dishonorable life.

719
01:08:50,108 --> 01:08:52,488
Living a dishonorable life...

720
01:08:53,519 --> 01:08:57,479
suits the ones like you, Vizier Alemşah.

721
01:09:03,341 --> 01:09:06,520
It is obvious that you are from
Yezidis (a community).

722
01:09:11,640 --> 01:09:14,041
We believe that...

723
01:09:15,850 --> 01:09:18,609
there is no victor other than Allah!

724
01:09:19,711 --> 01:09:26,401
And we do not bow before anyone but Allah.

725
01:09:27,841 --> 01:09:32,026
O Allah, the victor!

726
01:09:32,151 --> 01:09:34,551
O Allah, the victor!

727
01:09:35,459 --> 01:09:39,399
Reciting the kalima shahadah (confessing
his belief in Allah)

728
01:09:40,862 --> 01:09:45,421
Reciting the kalima shahadah (confessing
his belief in Allah)

729
01:09:59,186 --> 01:10:01,506
Come on, now! Come on!

730
01:10:12,124 --> 01:10:13,674
Eventually!

731
01:10:31,100 --> 01:10:32,860
Who did this?!

732
01:10:35,074 --> 01:10:36,988
Do you have a death wish?!

733
01:10:36,988 --> 01:10:39,368
Sultan Mesud did this, Vizier Alemşah.

734
01:10:45,191 --> 01:10:46,881
His order is certain.

735
01:10:57,805 --> 01:10:59,325
My Bey, we are alright.

736
01:10:59,325 --> 01:11:01,005
We are alright.

737
01:11:43,950 --> 01:11:45,680
How can it be possible?

738
01:11:46,779 --> 01:11:50,439
Osman is a rebel who tried to kill me.

739
01:11:52,453 --> 01:11:54,357
His death is obligatory.

740
01:11:54,357 --> 01:11:56,737
Sultan Mesud's order is certain.

741
01:11:58,160 --> 01:12:00,470
He wants him taken to Konya.

742
01:12:02,704 --> 01:12:04,874
If his death was obligatory...

743
01:12:05,647 --> 01:12:07,807
we wouldn't save him.

744
01:12:14,545 --> 01:12:20,575
Is a rebel's life more precious than the
life of the vizier of the Seljuk Empire?

745
01:12:20,988 --> 01:12:23,098
Is that why you prevented his death?

746
01:12:23,640 --> 01:12:25,570
The order is from the Sultan.

747
01:12:26,305 --> 01:12:29,895
Not fulfilling the order and killing
Osman here...

748
01:12:30,323 --> 01:12:32,643
which is a rebellious act...

749
01:12:33,643 --> 01:12:35,423
means opposing Sultan Mesud.

750
01:12:38,864 --> 01:12:40,904
In that case, I would take you...

751
01:12:42,119 --> 01:12:44,399
not Osman, Vizier Alemşah.

752
01:14:19,572 --> 01:14:23,992
You saved both my and my alps' life.

753
01:14:25,741 --> 01:14:27,301
Thank you.

754
01:14:27,772 --> 01:14:31,702
Our problem is not your
or your alps' life.

755
01:14:32,930 --> 01:14:38,250
Sultan Mesud wants to secure
justice in Konya.

756
01:14:50,551 --> 01:14:52,321
Where was justice...

757
01:14:53,302 --> 01:14:58,552
when Vizier Alemşah was doing
things that were full of lies against...

758
01:15:00,146 --> 01:15:02,106
Sultan Mesud all this time?

759
01:15:03,800 --> 01:15:06,440
Why Konya is too slow to act?

760
01:15:07,375 --> 01:15:10,535
The state arrives at its destination...

761
01:15:10,745 --> 01:15:12,445
neither early nor late.

762
01:15:13,688 --> 01:15:19,798
If we are here now, it is because the
state wanted us to be here now.

763
01:15:25,633 --> 01:15:27,603
Come on, we are going.

764
01:15:31,261 --> 01:15:33,541
You made a big mistake, Vizier
Alemşah.

765
01:15:33,715 --> 01:15:37,585
It is such a big mistake. When you had
the chance, you should've killed Osman.

766
01:15:37,657 --> 01:15:38,837
I told you to hurry!

767
01:16:00,111 --> 01:16:04,261
Where did this sergeant hear that
we were going to hang Osman?

768
01:16:13,206 --> 01:16:16,506
Vizier Alemşah is working
against the Sultan.

769
01:16:16,907 --> 01:16:20,957
He will hang Osman Bey without a
reason in the square of Bilecik.

770
01:16:22,175 --> 01:16:25,785
I know your problem so well,
Vizier Alemşah.

771
01:16:27,969 --> 01:16:30,589
But you will not be able to
achieve your goal.

772
01:16:31,432 --> 01:16:33,692
No one will know that I told you this.

773
01:16:35,407 --> 01:16:39,587
Even Osman Bey will think that he is saved
thanks to the order of Sultan Mesud.

774
01:16:43,755 --> 01:16:45,795
Don't worry.

775
01:16:46,196 --> 01:16:49,986
For the survival of the state, our
friends will not know our friendship...

776
01:16:52,000 --> 01:16:54,690
and our enemies will not know our
enmity.

777
01:16:58,114 --> 01:17:00,754
Get ready. We are going to Bilecik.

778
01:17:08,735 --> 01:17:12,895
That means the Sultan is watching
Bilecik too.

779
01:17:16,918 --> 01:17:21,578
I am the one who send him the news
from both here and Konya.

780
01:17:53,311 --> 01:17:55,651
There is a hidden catch here.

781
01:18:00,088 --> 01:18:02,068
And I will find that.

782
01:18:04,785 --> 01:18:06,915
But first, I'll take care of Osman.

783
01:18:06,915 --> 01:18:09,554
What Osman, Vizier Alemşah?!

784
01:18:09,554 --> 01:18:11,878
You'll take care of Osman?!

785
01:18:11,878 --> 01:18:14,308
He went away in front of our eyes!

786
01:18:15,882 --> 01:18:18,832
Don't be so sure, Agios Nikola.

787
01:18:22,555 --> 01:18:26,365
Osman will never be able to reach Konya.

788
01:18:43,823 --> 01:18:46,043
Miss, how will we escape?

789
01:18:47,100 --> 01:18:49,981
Landlord Koses and Turgut
Bey are not around.

790
01:18:49,981 --> 01:18:51,418
How will we escape?

791
01:18:51,418 --> 01:18:53,848
Don't be afraid, Cornelia. Don't be
afraid.

792
01:18:54,722 --> 01:18:58,052
They will not be able to do anything
to us if we are not afraid.

793
01:19:10,799 --> 01:19:12,399
Turgut!

794
01:19:24,522 --> 01:19:26,042
Come on!

795
01:19:44,084 --> 01:19:45,224
No!

796
01:19:46,338 --> 01:19:49,008
I will cut those hands that
touched my woman.

797
01:19:50,389 --> 01:19:51,869
Come.

798
01:20:31,033 --> 01:20:32,863
My Bey, they are coming!

799
01:20:36,828 --> 01:20:39,188
Alps, we are withdrawing!

800
01:20:39,295 --> 01:20:40,565
Cornelia, come here.

801
01:20:40,753 --> 01:20:41,913
Hurry up.

802
01:21:02,690 --> 01:21:04,580
Find them all!

803
01:21:05,231 --> 01:21:09,041
Consider yourself dead if you come
to İnegöl without finding them!

804
01:21:28,000 --> 01:21:29,610
Come on, alps!

805
01:21:30,318 --> 01:21:32,448
We are going to take Osman Bey.

806
01:21:32,753 --> 01:21:36,003
It is war day, it is hard to turn back.

807
01:21:36,173 --> 01:21:38,173
Those who can take the risk should come.

808
01:21:38,173 --> 01:21:40,124
The command is yours, Malhun Hatun.

809
01:22:10,940 --> 01:22:12,420
Come here.

810
01:22:16,888 --> 01:22:18,218
My Bey.

811
01:22:20,219 --> 01:22:22,744
Lord's soldiers lost track of us.

812
01:22:22,744 --> 01:22:24,124
Good.

813
01:22:27,031 --> 01:22:30,151
That Koses. What will I do with
your brother now, Mari?

814
01:22:30,526 --> 01:22:32,609
I told you that he is unreliable.

815
01:22:32,609 --> 01:22:35,129
It was not my brother this time, Turgut.

816
01:22:35,129 --> 01:22:36,929
His life is in danger too.

817
01:22:38,222 --> 01:22:40,512
My brothers and Osman Bey were caught.

818
01:22:41,810 --> 01:22:44,332
They will take my
brother to Constantinople.

819
01:22:44,332 --> 01:22:46,012
What are you talking about, Mari?

820
01:22:47,169 --> 01:22:48,669
Osman Bey too?

821
01:22:52,519 --> 01:22:54,469
Do you know where they keep them?

822
01:22:54,493 --> 01:22:55,823
I don't know.

823
01:22:56,054 --> 01:22:57,724
The vizier and Nikola.

824
01:22:58,048 --> 01:23:02,028
They seized the castle. What will
we do now?

825
01:23:02,705 --> 01:23:04,495
Okay. Keep calm.

826
01:23:05,009 --> 01:23:08,229
By the way, how did you learn that
I was kidnapped?

827
01:23:13,381 --> 01:23:16,921
You didn't have to come, my Bey.
We would collect the taxes.

828
01:23:17,961 --> 01:23:19,651
Thank you.

829
01:23:19,920 --> 01:23:21,990
But it's Osman Bey's order.

830
01:23:21,990 --> 01:23:23,830
How can I reject?

831
01:23:24,602 --> 01:23:27,712
I can't. Remember what Osman Bey
did for us.

832
01:23:28,618 --> 01:23:30,302
Alright.

833
01:23:30,302 --> 01:23:33,045
My Bey. Turgut Bey.

834
01:23:33,045 --> 01:23:34,585
What happened?

835
01:23:35,301 --> 01:23:38,641
Nikola came to the castle and seized it.
Mari Hatun is kidnapped.

836
01:23:39,272 --> 01:23:40,862
What are you talking about?

837
01:23:40,963 --> 01:23:42,993
They took her to İnegöl.

838
01:23:43,133 --> 01:23:44,473
Nikola.

839
01:23:45,046 --> 01:23:47,866
If you touch even a single
strand of her hair...

840
01:23:47,884 --> 01:23:50,234
I will tear you into pieces.

841
01:23:50,249 --> 01:23:52,079
Come on, alps!

842
01:23:52,186 --> 01:23:54,223
Don't worry, Mari.

843
01:23:54,223 --> 01:23:56,203
We will save your brother, Koses.

844
01:23:56,605 --> 01:23:58,545
And of course, Osman Bey too.

845
01:23:59,971 --> 01:24:01,921
I'm so glad that I have you.

846
01:24:02,334 --> 01:24:04,124
Firstly, Koses.

847
01:24:05,939 --> 01:24:08,909
It is obvious that Osman Bey
is in danger with his alps.

848
01:24:08,945 --> 01:24:12,835
Gündüz Bey and the vizier are
like a hand in the glove.

849
01:24:14,311 --> 01:24:17,201
You are saying that we need Kossess
and his soldiers, my Bey.

850
01:24:17,979 --> 01:24:20,059
Get ready, Kutan.

851
01:24:20,343 --> 01:24:23,883
We will save Osman Bey with Koses.

852
01:24:24,120 --> 01:24:25,650
As you ordered, my Bey.

853
01:24:26,236 --> 01:24:27,776
I will come too.

854
01:24:28,020 --> 01:24:29,390
No, Mari.

855
01:24:29,696 --> 01:24:31,256
What are you saying?

856
01:24:31,372 --> 01:24:34,042
Where will I go then, Turgut?

857
01:24:34,243 --> 01:24:38,043
To the place where I was kidnapped
or to the castle that Nİkola seized?

858
01:24:49,753 --> 01:24:51,573
Damn!

859
01:24:55,246 --> 01:24:57,386
How will I tell this to Nikola?

860
01:25:26,765 --> 01:25:31,245
There you go, brother! Run! Run! Run!

861
01:25:35,352 --> 01:25:37,062
Come on, brother!

862
01:25:57,759 --> 01:25:59,369
Osman Bey.

863
01:26:01,846 --> 01:26:04,916
We have already known that you
will do such a thing.

864
01:26:05,339 --> 01:26:07,219
Alright, only one was able to go.

865
01:26:09,376 --> 01:26:11,876
Has anyone heard that we do not
obey?

866
01:26:13,638 --> 01:26:14,968
Osman Bey.

867
01:26:15,460 --> 01:26:17,550
Osman Bey, we know you as a son
of a Bey...

868
01:26:18,008 --> 01:26:20,678
and respect you.

869
01:26:21,021 --> 01:26:25,083
And you should know that we are
the state and we saved...

870
01:26:25,083 --> 01:26:27,833
you from the rope in the name of Konya.

871
01:26:28,705 --> 01:26:32,335
We know you from your
ancestor, Ertuğrul Ghazi.

872
01:26:35,155 --> 01:26:37,025
We've been on the road for a long time.

873
01:26:37,055 --> 01:26:38,665
I didn't talk.

874
01:26:38,952 --> 01:26:41,052
Talking with a rebel is not
good behavior.

875
01:26:43,010 --> 01:26:46,450
But my ancestor Turan Bey
was used to talk about...

876
01:26:47,313 --> 01:26:52,203
your ancestor, Ertuğrul Ghazi.

877
01:26:55,682 --> 01:26:58,442
They fought together in many wars.

878
01:26:59,223 --> 01:27:03,143
Those who came to me always mentioned...

879
01:27:04,033 --> 01:27:06,483
the state first and then the respect.

880
01:27:07,702 --> 01:27:12,132
Sergeant İlgezdi, I don't trust anyone.

881
01:27:14,915 --> 01:27:19,645
Not every treacherous-looking person
will work against you, Osman Bey.

882
01:27:22,012 --> 01:27:24,332
It is like a good in the bad.

883
01:27:24,710 --> 01:27:27,330
Let's go to the presence of
the Sultan first.

884
01:27:28,849 --> 01:27:31,649
With his justice, you will be absolved
from guilt.

885
01:27:40,435 --> 01:27:42,115
Thank you.

886
01:27:43,425 --> 01:27:48,315
We do not forget the good or the bad.

887
01:27:51,661 --> 01:27:54,241
Soldiers, we are going.

888
01:28:39,425 --> 01:28:41,135
You stay there.

889
01:29:46,810 --> 01:29:50,160
I'm his killer slave.

890
01:29:51,528 --> 01:29:52,808
Come.

891
01:31:12,894 --> 01:31:14,344
Grapes.

892
01:31:33,344 --> 01:31:37,344
Vizier Alemşah.

893
01:31:59,191 --> 01:32:03,011
Loser dies.

894
01:32:11,425 --> 01:32:13,125
But...

895
01:32:14,758 --> 01:32:16,358
...I don't lose.

896
01:32:16,695 --> 01:32:18,415
No doubt.

897
01:32:28,106 --> 01:32:32,857
You are the leader of the armies that
make the bravest shake...

898
01:32:32,857 --> 01:32:37,517
...and break steel wrists, Geyhatu.

899
01:32:38,985 --> 01:32:41,205
I don't like talking too much.

900
01:32:45,475 --> 01:32:49,895
Did you kill Osman?

901
01:32:50,696 --> 01:32:52,376
No.

902
01:32:53,563 --> 01:32:55,593
I reserved him for you.

903
01:33:01,344 --> 01:33:03,524
He is under arrest now.

904
01:33:03,611 --> 01:33:05,271
He is going to Konya.

905
01:33:11,198 --> 01:33:16,268
But Osman can't reach Konya.
Whatever we must--

906
01:33:16,334 --> 01:33:18,104
He won't!

907
01:33:19,184 --> 01:33:22,304
But why? Does he know that...

908
01:33:22,604 --> 01:33:26,344
...we will dethrone the Sultan?

909
01:33:26,545 --> 01:33:31,855
No, Osman will find a way to cause
trouble.

910
01:33:38,272 --> 01:33:41,942
The sergeant who is bringing Osman
is a brave man.

911
01:33:42,760 --> 01:33:44,600
Be careful.

912
01:33:44,936 --> 01:33:49,376
Standing against a Mogul is difficult.

913
01:33:50,781 --> 01:33:55,431
How challenging can be a Seljuk soldier?

914
01:34:02,669 --> 01:34:06,519
They are using the road around
the Akman Mountain.

915
01:34:07,537 --> 01:34:10,307
Their horses must be tired now.

916
01:34:10,901 --> 01:34:13,441
They must spend the night at the cave.

917
01:34:54,255 --> 01:34:56,495
They will take my Osman Bey on his
way to Konya.

918
01:34:56,555 --> 01:34:58,595
But they are few people, my Sheik.

919
01:34:58,846 --> 01:35:01,876
I am afraid that something will happen.

920
01:35:01,995 --> 01:35:05,665
Malhun Hatun will catch up with Osman
Bey, if Allah lets.

921
01:35:05,750 --> 01:35:08,030
Don't worry, Bala Hatun.

922
01:35:11,430 --> 01:35:13,520
Osman Bey survived many hardships.

923
01:35:13,523 --> 01:35:15,663
He will get through this too, I hope.

924
01:35:16,213 --> 01:35:17,863
I hope.

925
01:35:31,927 --> 01:35:36,277
Wheat will certainly turn into ears.

926
01:35:42,875 --> 01:35:44,655
This is how it is...

927
01:35:45,754 --> 01:35:50,434
...wheat will go through
many difficult things...

928
01:35:51,149 --> 01:35:53,689
...until it mixes with the ground
and sprouts.

929
01:35:56,401 --> 01:36:00,271
It will be watered and grown
by the mercy of my Rabb.

930
01:36:03,466 --> 01:36:05,176
It will grow out to be a spike.

931
01:36:05,763 --> 01:36:09,543
Wind will blow, the sun will warm it up...

932
01:36:09,768 --> 01:36:13,558
...the day will come and that spike will
grow.

933
01:36:15,227 --> 01:36:18,557
And it will stand still.

934
01:36:20,939 --> 01:36:26,869
Are you saying Osman Bey is a seed
planted for these lands?

935
01:36:27,486 --> 01:36:29,376
Is that so?

936
01:36:29,478 --> 01:36:33,768
Is it easy to grow on the ground
and reach for the sky?

937
01:36:37,333 --> 01:36:40,733
It will be paninful.

938
01:36:41,576 --> 01:36:43,336
It will be big.

939
01:36:43,730 --> 01:36:50,020
We will say the earth is about to crack,
the seed is about to grow...

940
01:36:50,899 --> 01:36:55,469
...but Allah will tell us to wait.

941
01:36:56,386 --> 01:37:01,796
Wait, so your root gets stronger.

942
01:37:02,840 --> 01:37:06,400
Wait, so that your enemies can't hurt
you...

943
01:37:06,400 --> 01:37:10,010
...until you reach the sky.

944
01:37:12,810 --> 01:37:17,430
When poison ivy thinks it killed
you..

945
01:37:19,067 --> 01:37:23,507
...you will return stronger.

946
01:37:27,939 --> 01:37:29,759
Osman Bey.

947
01:37:30,554 --> 01:37:32,364
Osman Bey.

948
01:37:33,619 --> 01:37:38,289
His challenge is hard, his enemy is
evil.

949
01:37:38,740 --> 01:37:40,170
But...

950
01:37:40,342 --> 01:37:44,072
...the love in his heart...

951
01:37:44,705 --> 01:37:47,755
...will defeat all his enemies.

952
01:37:49,411 --> 01:37:54,461
This blessed cause will take over
these lands.

953
01:37:56,177 --> 01:38:00,997
Osman's generation will freely spread
the justice of Allah...

954
01:38:01,968 --> 01:38:06,608
...and the cause of the Prophet
to the whole world.

955
01:38:06,937 --> 01:38:08,337
I hope.

956
01:38:08,657 --> 01:38:10,547
Be of good cheer.

957
01:38:10,944 --> 01:38:13,984
This cause will not be left without
a leader.

958
01:38:16,247 --> 01:38:18,517
-I hope.
-I hope.

959
01:38:22,874 --> 01:38:24,704
Selamun Aleykum.

960
01:38:24,726 --> 01:38:26,906
Ve Aleykumselam.

961
01:38:27,557 --> 01:38:29,177
Aleykumselam.

962
01:38:29,777 --> 01:38:31,237
Mari?

963
01:38:31,741 --> 01:38:33,121
What happened?

964
01:38:33,326 --> 01:38:35,196
I don't have good news.

965
01:38:36,290 --> 01:38:40,890
Nowhere is safe. Thus, Turgut sent me
to you.

966
01:38:42,696 --> 01:38:46,396
You know about the tribe.
Nikola took over Harmankaya too.

967
01:38:49,164 --> 01:38:53,014
From now on, you are under our protection
my girl.

968
01:38:57,355 --> 01:38:59,775
Is there any news from Osman Bey?

969
01:39:19,032 --> 01:39:21,572
Aygül, you hold there.

970
01:39:21,998 --> 01:39:23,948
We will attack with my signal.

971
01:39:25,574 --> 01:39:28,214
Alaca and you will come with me.

972
01:39:30,278 --> 01:39:34,030
We will do whatever it takes to save
Osman Bey.

973
01:39:34,030 --> 01:39:36,370
As you order, Malhun Hatun.

974
01:39:36,794 --> 01:39:39,824
There will be a Kayı Tribe without us...

975
01:39:41,358 --> 01:39:43,548
...but not without Osman Bey!

976
01:39:44,117 --> 01:39:46,727
Come on! Let's go!

977
01:39:49,160 --> 01:39:50,320
Come on.

978
01:40:18,714 --> 01:40:20,744
They will go through this route.

979
01:40:20,918 --> 01:40:24,108
We will catch them here.

980
01:40:26,181 --> 01:40:28,151
But we are few.

981
01:40:28,571 --> 01:40:31,561
Too few.
We will be careful.

982
01:40:41,418 --> 01:40:43,048
Yes?

983
01:40:43,709 --> 01:40:46,899
My Bey, Vizier is taking Osman Bey
to Konya.

984
01:40:49,219 --> 01:40:51,299
I knew this would happen!

985
01:40:51,634 --> 01:40:55,974
Oh, Vizier! He will be strictly cautious
this time.

986
01:40:56,547 --> 01:40:58,467
Listen to me, alps!

987
01:40:58,657 --> 01:41:01,507
We need Kosses and his men for
Osman Bey.

988
01:41:01,517 --> 01:41:05,537
We will first save Kosses and then
Osman Bey.

989
01:41:05,854 --> 01:41:07,574
Yes, my Bey!

990
01:41:08,369 --> 01:41:10,519
What if we asked for the tribe's help,
my Bey?

991
01:41:10,926 --> 01:41:13,936
Gündüz Bey can't see the truth that
we see.

992
01:41:14,189 --> 01:41:17,719
Even if it's death in the end,
we'll handle this ourselves.

993
01:41:18,701 --> 01:41:21,835
Come on, valiants!
Let's go!

994
01:41:21,835 --> 01:41:23,515
Let's go!

995
01:41:55,107 --> 01:41:56,567
Alps!

996
01:41:57,899 --> 01:41:59,609
For Osman Bey!

997
01:42:08,353 --> 01:42:11,423
Let Osman Bey go!
We won't leave without him!

998
01:42:28,272 --> 01:42:29,635
Who are you?

999
01:42:29,635 --> 01:42:33,545
I am Malhun Hatun. Daughter of Umur Bey.
Hatun of Osman Bey.

1000
01:42:36,432 --> 01:42:37,982
Let my Bey go!

1001
01:42:41,433 --> 01:42:44,803
I am glad we met.

1002
01:42:45,262 --> 01:42:47,882
But we can't release Osman Bey.

1003
01:42:48,420 --> 01:42:50,550
The Sultan gave an order.

1004
01:42:51,558 --> 01:42:53,428
We have to go to Konya.

1005
01:42:53,694 --> 01:42:55,132
Come on, get out.

1006
01:42:55,132 --> 01:42:57,632
We won't return until we take Osman
Bey.

1007
01:42:57,677 --> 01:42:59,417
Alps!

1008
01:43:00,767 --> 01:43:04,727
Malhun Hatun, you are a few people.
Don't die for nothing.

1009
01:43:05,495 --> 01:43:07,925
We have a duty. Open the road.

1010
01:43:08,550 --> 01:43:11,990
You can keep your duty. I am taking
Osman Bey!

1011
01:43:13,255 --> 01:43:15,985
The easy way or the hard way.

1012
01:43:16,088 --> 01:43:18,578
-Alps!
-Malhun.

1013
01:43:21,948 --> 01:43:23,748
Stop for a second.

1014
01:43:27,039 --> 01:43:29,099
Stop for a second!

1015
01:43:37,465 --> 01:43:39,965
Fighting Turk to Turk doesn't suit us.

1016
01:43:41,421 --> 01:43:46,601
Especially spilling the blood of a Turk
because of me.

1017
01:43:57,312 --> 01:43:59,092
Do I have permission?

1018
01:43:59,941 --> 01:44:02,131
I want to talk to my Hatun.

1019
01:44:30,291 --> 01:44:31,721
Ah, Malhun, ah!

1020
01:44:35,385 --> 01:44:37,310
-My Bey.
-My Malhun.

1021
01:44:37,310 --> 01:44:39,140
Don't go, Osman.

1022
01:44:39,265 --> 01:44:41,455
We don't know what the Sultan will do.

1023
01:44:42,111 --> 01:44:45,221
I can't let you go like this.

1024
01:44:51,496 --> 01:44:53,196
Malhun.

1025
01:44:53,398 --> 01:44:55,218
We are outnumbered.

1026
01:44:55,642 --> 01:44:57,532
I have to go.

1027
01:44:59,232 --> 01:45:01,282
Otherwise, we will lose many valiants.

1028
01:45:03,339 --> 01:45:04,927
I can never let that happen.

1029
01:45:04,927 --> 01:45:06,167
My Bey.

1030
01:45:07,218 --> 01:45:11,248
I am afraid that Sultan may be under
the Vizier's influence.

1031
01:45:11,794 --> 01:45:13,994
What if he believed his lies?

1032
01:45:17,735 --> 01:45:19,485
Don't wor--

1033
01:45:36,095 --> 01:45:38,035
Don't worry.

1034
01:45:38,335 --> 01:45:42,775
With the help of my Mighty Rabb, I will
go to Konya and return.

1035
01:45:43,913 --> 01:45:50,933
After I return, they will pay for what
they have done to us!

1036
01:45:51,813 --> 01:45:53,288
Don't worry.

1037
01:45:53,288 --> 01:45:55,718
I hope, my Osman.
I hope.

1038
01:45:56,269 --> 01:45:58,269
But my only wish is...

1039
01:45:58,876 --> 01:46:02,476
...for you to take care of Bala
and Orhan.

1040
01:46:02,612 --> 01:46:04,562
Take care of each other.

1041
01:46:06,039 --> 01:46:08,279
Take care of the tribe.

1042
01:46:08,760 --> 01:46:11,140
I will, my Osman.

1043
01:46:13,510 --> 01:46:15,020
But...

1044
01:46:16,112 --> 01:46:17,742
...Gündüz Bey is gathering...

1045
01:46:17,884 --> 01:46:21,294
...the Assembly of Beys. What will we do
about that, my Bey?

1046
01:46:27,082 --> 01:46:28,822
That Gündüz Bey...

1047
01:46:30,906 --> 01:46:35,626
...will pay for sitting on Ertugrul Gazi's
seat.

1048
01:46:41,728 --> 01:46:46,138
Do whatever it takes to prevent him from
gathering the Assembly of Beys.

1049
01:46:49,779 --> 01:46:51,849
The only obstacle on the Turk's way...

1050
01:46:52,130 --> 01:46:53,920
...is Alemşah.

1051
01:46:54,972 --> 01:46:57,102
And he is working with him.

1052
01:46:58,237 --> 01:47:00,507
He is following his ways.

1053
01:47:01,602 --> 01:47:04,542
Güzdüz Bey is blind to the truth.

1054
01:47:06,278 --> 01:47:08,438
He can't sit on that throne.

1055
01:47:14,292 --> 01:47:16,492
What did they do to you?

1056
01:47:17,117 --> 01:47:18,977
It doesn't hurt.

1057
01:47:20,855 --> 01:47:22,485
Bless your right.

1058
01:47:24,504 --> 01:47:26,582
We may not return.

1059
01:47:26,582 --> 01:47:28,212
Don't say that!

1060
01:47:28,486 --> 01:47:30,496
Don't say that, Cerkutay.

1061
01:47:30,860 --> 01:47:34,950
Osman Bey and you will return safe and
sound.

1062
01:47:37,869 --> 01:47:39,719
I will wait for you.

1063
01:47:41,559 --> 01:47:43,139
Will you?

1064
01:47:44,530 --> 01:47:45,740
I will.

1065
01:47:48,628 --> 01:47:50,668
Osman Bey!

1066
01:47:51,564 --> 01:47:53,134
Come on!

1067
01:47:53,163 --> 01:47:55,253
We need to move on.

1068
01:48:16,718 --> 01:48:18,408
Be careful, my Osman.

1069
01:48:19,226 --> 01:48:21,226
Don't worry at all.

1070
01:48:24,058 --> 01:48:25,598
Come on.

1071
01:49:18,178 --> 01:49:19,878
Come on Alps!

1072
01:49:20,292 --> 01:49:22,312
We need to catch
the Assembly of Beys!

1073
01:49:22,366 --> 01:49:23,946
Come on!

1074
01:49:48,282 --> 01:49:50,212
Something happened.

1075
01:49:51,597 --> 01:49:53,147
I can tell.

1076
01:49:53,777 --> 01:49:55,517
What is it?

1077
01:49:58,101 --> 01:50:00,261
What is it?

1078
01:50:01,391 --> 01:50:02,931
Turgut...

1079
01:50:03,008 --> 01:50:04,138
So?

1080
01:50:04,198 --> 01:50:06,228
Ambushed us on our way to İnegöl.

1081
01:50:14,991 --> 01:50:16,701
They took Mari, Sir.

1082
01:50:18,537 --> 01:50:20,977
We tried to resist but we couldn't.

1083
01:50:22,865 --> 01:50:24,855
Most of the soldiers died.

1084
01:50:30,995 --> 01:50:33,174
Most of the soldiers died.

1085
01:50:33,174 --> 01:50:36,444
But you are alive.

1086
01:50:37,405 --> 01:50:39,007
Right, Argus?

1087
01:50:39,007 --> 01:50:42,007
Huh? Idiot Argus!

1088
01:50:42,008 --> 01:50:44,268
Good for nothing Argus!

1089
01:51:08,714 --> 01:51:11,114
Since he got Mari...

1090
01:51:11,851 --> 01:51:14,041
...his move is clear.

1091
01:51:15,000 --> 01:51:16,640
Kosses.

1092
01:51:17,576 --> 01:51:19,546
And where is Kosses?

1093
01:51:19,736 --> 01:51:22,306
On the Constantinople way.

1094
01:51:27,365 --> 01:51:29,155
On the horses!

1095
01:51:52,192 --> 01:51:55,172
You didn't leave me for more money.

1096
01:51:56,085 --> 01:51:58,295
I am grateful to you.

1097
01:51:58,422 --> 01:52:02,512
We are sorry we couldn't prevent this
disgrace, Lord Rogatus.

1098
01:52:02,621 --> 01:52:03,701
No, no.

1099
01:52:05,155 --> 01:52:07,315
It is no time to talk about the past.

1100
01:52:08,405 --> 01:52:09,775
Nikola...

1101
01:52:11,034 --> 01:52:12,474
...Vizier...

1102
01:52:13,191 --> 01:52:15,611
...whoever betrayed me...

1103
01:52:16,850 --> 01:52:19,648
...we will make them all pay.

1104
01:52:19,648 --> 01:52:23,258
We are here for this, Sir. We'll do
whatever you need.

1105
01:52:24,046 --> 01:52:25,706
Now, return to the castle.

1106
01:52:26,591 --> 01:52:29,831
Continue to act as if you are not aware
of anything.

1107
01:52:29,844 --> 01:52:31,994
I am going to Constantinople.

1108
01:52:32,151 --> 01:52:34,091
I will return with good news.

1109
01:52:59,495 --> 01:53:01,005
Thank you.

1110
01:53:02,790 --> 01:53:05,070
Come on, enjoy!

1111
01:53:05,137 --> 01:53:06,657
Alps!

1112
01:53:08,879 --> 01:53:10,319
Enjoy!

1113
01:53:30,838 --> 01:53:33,318
You are very willing to take us.

1114
01:53:34,877 --> 01:53:37,417
Do you trust the state of Konya?

1115
01:53:37,654 --> 01:53:40,544
There is not much to worry, Osman Bey.

1116
01:53:41,916 --> 01:53:44,656
A fading star.

1117
01:53:49,856 --> 01:53:52,006
Why are we going then?

1118
01:53:53,074 --> 01:53:57,094
I trust Sultan Mesud. You get clear
with his justice so that...

1119
01:53:57,429 --> 01:54:01,639
...a new star can shine.

1120
01:54:05,630 --> 01:54:08,100
But the Vizier...

1121
01:54:09,794 --> 01:54:12,024
...is confusing the Sultan.

1122
01:54:13,807 --> 01:54:16,337
He is the same as a snake.

1123
01:54:18,395 --> 01:54:20,075
Venomous.

1124
01:54:22,836 --> 01:54:25,866
The fate of the snake we catch
is obvious.

1125
01:54:27,197 --> 01:54:31,327
He will pay for what he's done too.

1126
01:54:31,569 --> 01:54:35,029
The power to make them pay is within
the Kayı!

1127
01:54:35,634 --> 01:54:37,324
Why?

1128
01:54:40,763 --> 01:54:42,833
Why do you trust us?

1129
01:54:48,642 --> 01:54:51,772
Are you the only Kayı people, huh?

1130
01:54:56,644 --> 01:54:58,754
Kayı is everywhere.

1131
01:54:58,972 --> 01:55:01,302
Serving the same purpose.

1132
01:55:01,933 --> 01:55:04,183
Liberty of the Turks!

1133
01:55:17,290 --> 01:55:20,880
Sultan Mesud's order is above anything.

1134
01:55:22,250 --> 01:55:27,030
Otherwise, I would be throwing
swords with you now.

1135
01:55:32,090 --> 01:55:34,120
When I get clear...

1136
01:55:34,269 --> 01:55:35,879
...we will.

1137
01:55:37,104 --> 01:55:39,574
We will.

1138
01:55:39,985 --> 01:55:41,785
Thank you.

1139
01:55:47,036 --> 01:55:49,286
I promised Vizier Alemşah.

1140
01:55:50,341 --> 01:55:52,151
The Assembly will take place tomorrow!

1141
01:56:08,648 --> 01:56:10,608
What are you doing, Hatuns?

1142
01:56:11,075 --> 01:56:13,475
What are you doing, Gündüz Bey?

1143
01:56:14,669 --> 01:56:19,119
We brought news from the Bey of Kayı.

1144
01:56:23,514 --> 01:56:25,424
Who is it?

1145
01:56:25,881 --> 01:56:28,131
Osman is prisoned, Bala Hatun.

1146
01:56:28,359 --> 01:56:29,659
Güzdüz Bey...

1147
01:56:30,655 --> 01:56:35,175
...you forgot but the actual owner
of the throne is Osman Bey.

1148
01:56:38,901 --> 01:56:41,331
We met with my Bey on his way to Konya.

1149
01:56:45,847 --> 01:56:47,817
Osman Bey says that no matter...

1150
01:56:47,924 --> 01:56:51,354
...what the price is, I will return to my
tribe!

1151
01:56:52,533 --> 01:56:56,483
He said he will sit on the throne
he took from Ertuğrul Gazi again.

1152
01:56:57,740 --> 01:57:02,020
And he said that he will behead anyone if
he...

1153
01:57:02,437 --> 01:57:04,837
...is sitting there when he returns.

1154
01:57:07,241 --> 01:57:09,381
My valiant...

1155
01:57:09,912 --> 01:57:11,902
...Osman Bey!

1156
01:57:12,389 --> 01:57:15,729
He doesn't leave his tribe!

1157
01:57:17,500 --> 01:57:22,520
Would Kayı Tribe ever suffer when it
has such a Bey?

1158
01:57:23,725 --> 01:57:26,695
If Osman Bey said so, he will return.

1159
01:57:26,967 --> 01:57:28,365
Osman Bey will come back!

1160
01:57:28,365 --> 01:57:30,955
We need Osman Bey for the sake of
the tribe!

1161
01:57:34,091 --> 01:57:36,281
It is the order of the Vizier!

1162
01:57:36,559 --> 01:57:38,559
The Assembly will take place!

1163
01:57:38,832 --> 01:57:42,742
Osman Bey's order, the Assembly
will not take place!

1164
01:57:44,043 --> 01:57:46,683
My Bey is not here, but we are.

1165
01:57:46,986 --> 01:57:48,696
We won't let it happen!

1166
01:57:49,840 --> 01:57:51,660
It is the order of the state!

1167
01:57:52,725 --> 01:57:55,155
Everyone will obey!

1168
01:57:58,210 --> 01:57:59,890
You too!

1169
01:58:02,320 --> 01:58:04,770
Osman included!

1170
01:58:09,798 --> 01:58:13,408
If anyone can, let them come...

1171
01:58:15,168 --> 01:58:16,808
...and stop us.

1172
01:58:30,051 --> 01:58:31,421
Brothers...

1173
01:58:31,705 --> 01:58:33,045
...we may not but...

1174
01:58:34,492 --> 01:58:36,392
...my Bey has a dream...

1175
01:58:37,372 --> 01:58:41,362
...but they do anything to stop him.

1176
01:58:43,176 --> 01:58:45,306
How could this happen?

1177
01:58:45,817 --> 01:58:48,447
We just escaped the ropes.

1178
01:58:49,950 --> 01:58:52,890
About Konya, we don't know what
will happen.

1179
01:58:53,893 --> 01:58:55,653
May Allah help us.

1180
01:58:55,749 --> 01:58:57,279
Amen.

1181
01:58:58,658 --> 01:59:02,278
If it is up to Allah, then it is done,
brothers.

1182
01:59:03,072 --> 01:59:06,162
My Bey will get out of this trouble.

1183
01:59:06,467 --> 01:59:08,327
Of course.

1184
01:59:08,360 --> 01:59:11,010
But how, brother?

1185
01:59:11,988 --> 01:59:14,688
My Bey is such a bey that...

1186
01:59:15,927 --> 01:59:18,817
... he helped many, he saved many.

1187
01:59:19,694 --> 01:59:23,994
Of course, he bothers the tyrants.

1188
01:59:25,074 --> 01:59:27,164
He does.

1189
01:59:27,995 --> 01:59:31,215
That's why they play many games
to him, they slander him.

1190
01:59:32,623 --> 01:59:34,253
Therefore...

1191
01:59:34,723 --> 01:59:38,530
...what we must do is stay strong...

1192
01:59:38,530 --> 01:59:40,170
...without a doubt.

1193
01:59:41,884 --> 01:59:44,004
This will all end, if Allah lets.

1194
01:59:45,848 --> 01:59:49,668
My homeland is also crushed under
the Mongol persecution.

1195
01:59:49,842 --> 01:59:53,192
Welcome, brother.

1196
01:59:53,327 --> 01:59:58,217
We are glad but why did you come?

1197
01:59:59,188 --> 02:00:01,438
Hope is here, brother.

1198
02:00:01,906 --> 02:00:04,046
Hope is within Osman Bey.

1199
02:00:04,659 --> 02:00:06,529
He leads the fight.

1200
02:00:07,194 --> 02:00:11,544
Wherever Jihad is, the Muslim
considers it homeland.

1201
02:00:14,989 --> 02:00:17,669
Mashallah to my brother!

1202
02:00:18,682 --> 02:00:22,112
When we get through these days and I
get my swords back...

1203
02:00:23,134 --> 02:00:25,684
...we will fight many battles, I hope.

1204
02:00:26,271 --> 02:00:27,581
Thank you.

1205
02:00:28,634 --> 02:00:32,704
Thanks to my Allah for getting our paths
together.

1206
02:00:32,817 --> 02:00:34,917
Thank you, brother.

1207
02:00:35,068 --> 02:00:38,108
Thank you, brother.
Thank you.

1208
02:00:43,095 --> 02:00:46,785
Seljuks and Osman are in the cave.

1209
02:00:47,423 --> 02:00:50,673
We can go and rip off their heads.

1210
02:00:50,969 --> 02:00:55,389
How many soldiers are around the cave?

1211
02:00:55,595 --> 02:00:57,305
Many.

1212
02:00:57,794 --> 02:01:02,474
A cave is a good place to defend.

1213
02:01:03,263 --> 02:01:09,193
They may resist. We will wait for them
to leave the cave in the morning.

1214
02:01:11,151 --> 02:01:14,121
We will hit them on the road.

1215
02:01:14,121 --> 02:01:19,641
Then, you
can rip off as many heads as you want.

1216
02:01:20,858 --> 02:01:24,518
Is Osman's gift well?

1217
02:01:26,592 --> 02:01:28,272
For now.

1218
02:01:29,670 --> 02:01:31,010
Good.

1219
02:01:34,167 --> 02:01:37,047
Osman is a brave man.

1220
02:01:37,668 --> 02:01:42,308
But he is an obstacle for my goals.

1221
02:01:44,218 --> 02:01:46,028
He will be gone.

1222
02:01:54,042 --> 02:01:55,512
Osman.

1223
02:01:57,505 --> 02:02:00,005
I need Alemşah.

1224
02:02:00,754 --> 02:02:03,424
And he needs your death.

1225
02:02:06,805 --> 02:02:09,685
Argun Han will die.

1226
02:02:11,751 --> 02:02:14,551
Sultan Mesud will die.

1227
02:02:14,963 --> 02:02:17,363
You will die.

1228
02:02:18,026 --> 02:02:21,016
The Khan of all these lands...

1229
02:02:22,257 --> 02:02:24,417
...will be me!

1230
02:02:45,601 --> 02:02:47,151
You!

1231
02:03:13,254 --> 02:03:14,934
Brother!

1232
02:03:33,058 --> 02:03:34,508
Brother!

1233
02:04:17,384 --> 02:04:18,734
My Bey!

1234
02:04:18,734 --> 02:04:20,304
Brother.

1235
02:04:24,375 --> 02:04:26,055
Are you all right, my Bey?

1236
02:04:32,466 --> 02:04:35,586
The Sergeant is waiting outside, my Bey.

1237
02:04:43,664 --> 02:04:45,344
Brother.

1238
02:04:47,156 --> 02:04:49,956
My brother won't sit on the throne.

1239
02:04:51,510 --> 02:04:53,990
Let alone the state we will establish...

1240
02:04:54,624 --> 02:04:57,434
...he wants to destroy the existing one.

1241
02:05:00,879 --> 02:05:02,069
My Bey.

1242
02:05:02,945 --> 02:05:05,005
There is Malhun Hatun...

1243
02:05:05,369 --> 02:05:07,069
...Bala Hatun.

1244
02:05:07,770 --> 02:05:11,240
Selcen Mother, Aygül.

1245
02:05:11,889 --> 02:05:16,269
There is Göktuğ brother, my Bey.
He will of course go to the tribe.

1246
02:05:16,362 --> 02:05:17,796
They will stop them, my Bey.

1247
02:05:17,796 --> 02:05:21,606
Yes, Cerkutay. The hatuns will stop him.

1248
02:05:22,718 --> 02:05:24,298
They will.

1249
02:05:24,846 --> 02:05:26,616
The throne...

1250
02:05:26,829 --> 02:05:28,519
...will wait for its real owner.

1251
02:05:30,162 --> 02:05:32,041
There is also Turgut Bey!

1252
02:05:32,231 --> 02:05:36,211
He will come for us as soon as he hears
about us, my Bey.

1253
02:05:36,305 --> 02:05:38,485
Yes, he is our brother.

1254
02:06:41,752 --> 02:06:43,382
Kosses!

1255
02:06:44,190 --> 02:06:47,130
Where are you going without avenging
your sister?

1256
02:07:13,446 --> 02:07:15,966
Let no one touch his sword so that...

1257
02:07:17,245 --> 02:07:21,335
...women do not become widows
and children orphans.

1258
02:07:31,503 --> 02:07:32,833
Come on!

1259
02:07:57,274 --> 02:07:58,854
Just in time!

1260
02:08:21,609 --> 02:08:24,459
Look who is here!

1261
02:08:26,995 --> 02:08:31,425
As Turgut Bey said, don't touch your
swords.

1262
02:08:32,001 --> 02:08:34,919
Otherwise Mari will both become
a widow and...

1263
02:08:35,349 --> 02:08:38,209
...what do you call a person whose
brother is dead?

1264
02:08:38,330 --> 02:08:39,880
You!

1265
02:08:40,719 --> 02:08:43,039
I don't know. It doesn't matter.

1266
02:08:56,359 --> 02:08:58,349
Tragedy.

1267
02:09:03,692 --> 02:09:05,492
I love it.

1268
02:10:10,454 --> 02:10:12,214
Geyhatu!

1269
02:10:12,423 --> 02:10:13,733
Osman...

1270
02:10:14,660 --> 02:10:17,080
...we met again!

1271
02:10:20,385 --> 02:10:24,325
I stopped you for a gift.

1272
02:10:26,813 --> 02:10:28,203
Bring him!

1273
02:10:35,248 --> 02:10:36,838
Göktuğ!

1274
02:10:38,750 --> 02:10:40,580
Brother!

1275
02:10:42,609 --> 02:10:44,599
Göktuğ!

1276
02:10:45,916 --> 02:10:47,536
My Bey!

1277
02:11:35,228 --> 02:11:37,238
Kongar or Göktuğ!

1278
02:11:38,360 --> 02:11:40,350
He was a Mogul!

1279
02:11:41,995 --> 02:11:45,075
He grew up like a Mongolian!

1280
02:11:45,480 --> 02:11:49,160
You turned him into a Turk!

1281
02:11:51,976 --> 02:11:56,716
This makes you a good leader and a
dangerous enemy.

1282
02:12:01,519 --> 02:12:04,529
You will die, Osman!

1283
02:12:07,103 --> 02:12:09,633
But first...

1284
02:12:11,481 --> 02:12:13,151
...this traitor.

1285
02:12:16,457 --> 02:12:21,997
Every heart that beats for rebellion
is doomed to be pierced.

1286
02:12:23,970 --> 02:12:25,750
Don't you dare!

1287
02:12:27,644 --> 02:12:30,194
If you pierce his heart...

1288
02:12:30,871 --> 02:12:35,651
...the fire for revenge in me and in every
Turk...

1289
02:12:35,952 --> 02:12:38,272
...will burn you alive!

1290
02:12:43,033 --> 02:12:44,523
My Bey!

1291
02:12:46,021 --> 02:12:48,131
Geyhatu thinks...

1292
02:12:48,860 --> 02:12:51,150
...he can break us.

1293
02:12:52,694 --> 02:12:54,764
But we come alive the more we die!

1294
02:12:56,470 --> 02:12:58,740
Death is inevitable.

1295
02:13:01,575 --> 02:13:02,875
But...

1296
02:13:03,536 --> 02:13:05,426
...dying with my brothers...

1297
02:13:06,271 --> 02:13:10,181
...and my Bey on the right path...

1298
02:13:12,663 --> 02:13:14,713
... is my consolation.

1299
02:13:17,286 --> 02:13:21,726
A death like this can only strengthen us.

1300
02:13:29,708 --> 02:13:31,628
-No!
-Göktuğ!

1301
02:13:34,143 --> 02:13:35,573
No!

1302
02:13:39,496 --> 02:13:41,076
Göktuğ!

1303
02:13:42,370 --> 02:13:43,890
Brother!

1304
02:13:43,959 --> 02:13:45,439
Geyhatu!

1305
02:13:49,153 --> 02:13:50,743
Brother!

1306
02:13:52,901 --> 02:13:54,189
Let me go!

1307
02:13:54,189 --> 02:13:59,099
I bear witness that there is
no god but Allah...

1308
02:14:00,788 --> 02:14:03,238
No! Göktuğ!

1309
02:14:03,484 --> 02:14:05,394
Göktuğ!

1310
02:14:06,562 --> 02:14:10,312
...and I bear witness that Muhammad--

1311
02:14:23,831 --> 02:14:25,421
You dog!

1312
02:14:38,431 --> 02:14:40,421
... is the servant and Messenger
of Allah.

1313
02:14:48,095 --> 02:14:49,165
Brother!

1314
02:14:56,550 --> 02:14:58,400
Göktuğ!

1315
02:14:58,802 --> 02:15:00,932
Göktuğ! My brother!

1316
02:15:01,040 --> 02:15:03,130
Göktuğ!

1317
02:15:05,860 --> 02:15:07,680
Göktuğ!

1318
